{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014di9iH6ixo6GJxEnNZGux8","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive picture. Let me create a detailed summary report.\n\n## Final Report: Experiment Details, Metrics, Results, and Configuration\n\nI have conducted a very thorough search of `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17` and found all relevant experiment files, configuration, and metadata. Here's the complete summary:\n\n### PROJECTS OVERVIEW\n\n**Two active projects:**\n1. **recovery_aware_struct_prune** - Recovery-Aware Structured Pruning for reasoning models (EMNLP 2026)\n2. **schema-conform-ie-training** - Schema-conformant IE training with GRPO (schema-conform task)\n\n---\n\n## PROJECT 1: recovery_aware_struct_prune\n\n**Key Files:**\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/experiment_plan.yaml` (18 planned experiments, 8 with REGISTRY_ID)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/registry.yaml` (33 experiments tracked with full details)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/dream_registry.yaml` (2 dream reviews, best/median/worst scenarios)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/paper_framing.md` (59 lines of core narrative)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/writing_plan.yaml` (323 lines of paper structure)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/memory.md` (42 lines of key findings and constraints)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/decisions.yaml` (300+ decision records)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/constraints.yaml` (3 GPU/disk constraints)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/docs/IDEA_BRIEF.md` (177 lines, seed topic and reviewer feedback)\n\n**Core Research Question:**\nDoes CKA-based functional overlap predict RLVR recoverability better than standard importance-only pruning? Tested on DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B with 20% structured sparsity.\n\n**Main Results (as of 2026-05-15):**\n\n| Stage | RASP 20% | Standard 20% | Gap | Status |\n|-------|----------|-------------|-----|--------|\n| Post-prune (N=100) | 29% | 1% | **28pp (p<0.0001)** | DONE |\n| +SFT warmup (N=100) | 57% | 64% | -7pp (Standard higher) | DONE |\n| +GRPO Stage 2 | [TBD - v7 8-bit optimizer running] | [running] | [pending] | RUNNING |\n\n**Experiment Registry (33 entries):**\n\nCore MVP experiments:\n- `mvp_rasp_pipeline_v4`: Dual sparsity probe (20%/25%), RASP=29% vs Standard=1% ✓ DONE\n- `sft_rasp_20`: SFT warmup on RASP model → 57% accuracy, 99% EOS rate ✓ DONE\n- `sft_standard_20`: SFT warmup on Standard model → 64% accuracy, 99% EOS rate ✓ DONE\n- `grpo_stage2_rasp_20_v7`: GRPO recovery with 8-bit AdamW (cuda:0) ▶ RUNNING\n- `grpo_stage2_standard_20_v7`: GRPO recovery parallel (cuda:1) ▶ RUNNING\n\nAblation experiments:\n- `alpha_ablation_westd_cal256`: α ∈ {0.0, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 4.0} at 20% sparsity\n  - α=4.0 achieved 40% post-prune (best), α=1.0 (default RASP) = 29% post-prune\n  - SFT recovery: α=4.0 → 62% accuracy (57% for α=1.0) — non-monotonic relationship\n\nBaseline experiments:\n- `grasp_baseline_westd`: GRASPrune baseline → 8% post-prune (50 samples), 3.6x gap vs RASP 29%\n- `sft_grasp_20_westd`: GraSP + SFT recovery (in progress)\n\nComparative evals:\n- `reeval_postprune_definitive`: westb (RASP 31% vs Standard 27%, 4pp gap) + westd validation\n\n**Key Findings from Memory & Decisions:**\n\n1. **Calibration sensitivity** (D022): westb (512 cal samples) vs westd (256 cal samples) → ~5% MLP group selection difference → fragile threshold at 20% sparsity\n2. **GRPO sampling collapse** (D019): SFT restores greedy accuracy (57-64%) and EOS (99%), but GRPO sampling (temp=0.7) still produces repetitive loops; v6/v7 using 8-bit optimizer to fit in GPU memory\n3. **GraSP validation** (memory): GraSP 8% << RASP 29-31%, confirming CKA-aware advantage over gradient saliency\n4. **SFT > GRPO apparent reversal** (D015): Standard 64% > RASP 57% at SFT stage, but this is Claim 3 evidence (recovery method affects pruning order), not a failure\n\n**Paper Constraints:**\n\n- **Dual-version narrative** (writing_plan.yaml): \n  - Strong version: GRPO confirms RASP >> Standard (all 3 claims)\n  - Weak version: Focus on post-prune evidence + interaction analysis (claims 1-2)\n- **Evidence restrictions**: SFT N=100 gap (57% vs 64%) has overlapping CI, cannot support ordering reversal claim (ER-001)\n- **Writing order**: method → related_work → introduction → experiments → abstract → conclusion\n\n**Experimental Constraints (constraints.yaml):**\n\n| ID | Constraint | Scope | Reason |\n|----|-----------|-------|--------|\n| C001 | GPU whitelist: westb-23072 cuda:0/1 only | all | Shared server, prevent overflow |\n| C002 | All files → /root/autodl-tmp/, no root partition | worker | Root partition 30GB, v4 failed when full |\n| C003 | westd-11672 cuda:0/1 exclusive to this project | all | New allocation (2×RTX PRO 6000) |\n\n**Hardware & Status:**\n- Model: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B (28 layers, GQA 28Q/4KV, 7B params)\n- Data: GSM8K (7473 train, 1319 test), MATH-500\n- Servers: westb-23072 (primary), westd-11672 (ablations)\n- GPU hours consumed: ~150h (MVP + SFT + baseline work); GRPO v7 active\n\n**Dream Review Results (dream_20260514T233950):**\n- Best tier: 4/6 contributions\n- Median tier: 3/6 contributions  \n- Worst tier: 3/6 contributions\n- Action items: plan_015 (α ablation, P0), plan_016 (inference speedup, P1), plan_017 (unstructured baseline, P1)\n- Reviews identify critical gaps: α ablation, single model, missing inference speedup, multi-seed validation\n\n**Paper Progress:**\n- Outline: 8-page EMNLP submission (deadline May 25, 2026 ARR)\n- Sections drafted: method, related_work (pending full literature search), introduction (conditional on GRPO results)\n- Figures blocked: fig2_accuracy_comparison, fig4_recovery_trajectory (awaiting GRPO Stage 2)\n- Table 1 (main results) status: [TBD] placeholders for GRPO recovery columns\n\n---\n\n## PROJECT 2: schema-conform-ie-training\n\n**Key Files:**\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/schema-conform-ie-training/registry.yaml` (200+ lines, 8 experiments)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/schema-conform-ie-training/memory.md` (33 lines, key findings)\n\n**Experiment Results:**\n\n| Exp | Model | Task | F1-Correctness | Structural Validity | Status |\n|-----|-------|------|---|---|---|\n| exp_001 (baseline) | Qwen3.5-9B + LoRA | GRPO F1-only | 0.2725 (scierc) | 1.0 | ✓ DONE |\n| exp_002 (conformance) | Qwen3.5-9B + LoRA | GRPO 5-comp + GDPO | 0.2244 (scierc) | 0.9764 | ✓ DONE |\n| eval_C_v2 (base zero-shot) | Qwen3.5-9B | Pretrained baseline | 0.2184 (scierc) | 0.9964 | ✓ DONE |\n| exp_004_d1_v2+ | [Multiple ablations tracking F1-dominant weighting] | | | | PREPARING |\n\n**Key Findings (memory.md):**\n- Conformance reward does NOT improve zero-shot transfer (CrossNER gap <0.5pp)\n- Conformance improves schema adherence (relational_constraint +20.7pp) but damages relation_f1 (-5.72pp)\n- D1 v4 (F1-dominant 75:25, no GDPO) is most efficient: 500 steps → entity_f1=0.4966, relation_f1=0.2913\n- Multi-step training benefits: A(500)→A-cont(900)→A-cont(1000): entity_f1 0.4404→0.5158→0.5172\n\n---\n\n## GLOBAL LOGS & REGISTRIES\n\n**Main Global Registry:**\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/global/logs/workers/registry.json` (worker job tracking)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/global/logs/registry_audit.jsonl` (audit log)\n\n**System Logs:**\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/global/logs/system.log` (system events)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/global/logs/session_events.jsonl` (session tracking)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/global/logs/usage.jsonl` + `.lock` (usage tracking)\n\n**Idea Generator:**\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/idea_generator/ideas.yaml` (ideation state)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/idea_generator/ideas.lock` (lock file)\n\n**Worker Logs (recovery_aware_struct_prune):**\n- 100+ worker log files in `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/logs/workers/` tracking:\n  - MVP pipeline stages (prune, eval, GRPO, SFT)\n  - Fixes and debugging (OOM resolution, path corrections)\n  - Baseline setup (GRASP model prep, code sync)\n  - Training operations (status checks, monitoring)\n\n**Dream Reports:**\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T233950/`:\n  - `best/`, `median/`, `worst/` folders containing:\n    - `experiment_data.json` (reviewer scenario data)\n    - `paper_framing.md` (narrative per tier)\n    - `imagined_experiments.yaml` (hypothetical experiments)\n    - `review_context.yaml` (context for reviews)\n    - `paper.log` + `logs/` (paper agent execution logs)\n\n---\n\n## CONFIGURATION FILES\n\n**YAML Configs:**\n\n| File | Purpose | Key Config |\n|------|---------|-----------|\n| `config/approvals.yaml` | Approval workflow | Project approval thresholds |\n| `config/backend.yaml` | Backend configuration | Workers, queues, logging |\n| `config/resources.yaml` | Resource allocation | GPU budgets, memory limits |\n| `config/crons.yaml` | Scheduled jobs | Recurring checks, maintenance |\n| `config/feishu.yaml` | Feishu (DingTalk) webhook | Notification integration |\n| `workspace.yaml` | Workspace settings | Global project settings |\n\n**Project-specific YAML:**\n- `projects/rec