hold up. I'm also reconsidering plan_005 with GRASPrune—the baseline numbers look concerning with only 8% accuracy on 50 samples and a 2% EOS rate, which mirrors the original Standard problem. That low EOS rate might be masking even worse underlying reasoning performance, so I need to think through what role GRASPrune actually plays in the best tier narrative.\n\nFor GRASPrune to meaningfully rule out the idea that recovery is just a function of post-prune accuracy, it needs to show a different recovery pattern than Standard despite having much lower post-prune performance. If GRASPrune bottoms out at 10% post-prune but bounces back to 38% after GRPO—a 28 percentage point gain—while Standard goes from 27% to 53% for a 26 point gain, that's interesting because GRASPrune recovers more despite starting much lower. But then RASP's trajectory of 31% to 70% gives an even larger 39 point gain, which complicates the ordering I'm trying to establish.\n\nLooking at the actual correlation between post-prune accuracy and recovery gains, the pattern breaks down: RASP at 31% post-prune gains 39 points, Standard at 27% gains 26 points, and GRASPrune at just 10% gains 28 points. If recovery were simply determined by post-prune accuracy, I'd expect a monotonic relationship where higher starting accuracy predicts higher gains, but GRASPrune's 28-point gain contradicts that—it outperforms Standard despite being far behind in post-prune performance. This suggests GRASPrune's learned representations have some property that makes them particularly amenable to GRPO recovery.\n\nThe key difference is that GRASPrune's gates, though producing lower immediate accuracy, preserve structural diversity that GRPO can exploit for redistribution. Standard's Taylor importance metric tends to keep \"important\" structures that are often redundant and overlapping, leaving less room for GRPO to explore and recover. This is a compelling narrative for the paper.\n\nCompiling the full results across all methods...\n\nLooking at the post-GRPO rankings, RASP dominates at 70%, followed by unstructured at 60%, then standard at 53%. The interesting insight is that RASP's structured pruning outperforms unstructured despite removing entire components—because it preserves functionally distinct structures that GRPO can effectively optimize, whereas unstructured pruning weakens all structures uniformly, creating lower-quality substrates for the redistribution process.\n\nNow I'm compiling the scoring ablation results for plan_007, comparing different importance metrics: the full RASP formulation combining information content and functional uniqueness, CKA-only variants, gradient-based Taylor importance, magnitude-only pruning, and random baselines. The key takeaway is that RASP's 70% performance with 1.28x inference speedup represents the practical sweet spot—beating unstructured methods while delivering concrete efficiency gains. The post-prune comparison is what matters for isolating CKA's contribution, so I'll stick with those numbers. Now I'm writing out the full YAML structure for all 18 experiments, making sure to track dependencies—like how plan_004 and plan_008 both depend on plan_003's GRPO recovery completing successfully. I should also weave the recovery amplification story into the narrative guidance at the top to frame why these results matter.\n\nWriting YAML structure...\n\nI need to distinguish plan_009 (extended SFT with full compute budget) from plan_002 (warmup SFT with limited compute). Extended SFT should show marginal improvements over warmup—RASP around 58% and Standard around 66%—since additional training yields diminishing returns.\n\nNow I'm finalizing the YAML structure with the best-tier configuration and narrative framing that explains how GRPO amplifies post-pruning differences into a recovery gap, where RASP's structural uniqueness enables better redistribution while Standard's high overlap paradoxically becomes a liability under GRPO despite performing well under SFT alone.\n\nI'm also planning the full GSM8K evaluation with the complete dataset to validate these findings across the board. 现在看到完整的N=1319评估结果，RASP和Standard的性能差距只有4个百分点，而置信区间从N=100时的±9pp收窄到±2.5pp，McNemar检验的p值0.0038证实了这个差异的统计显著性。关键洞察是这不是之前认为的29倍优势，而是保留率约1.15倍的差异，真正的放大效应来自后续GRPO阶段，post-prune的4pp差距本身只是必要条件而非充分条件。\n\n两种方法在20%结构化剪枝下保留了相似总量的推理能力，但保留的结构组成截然不同——RASP倾向保留功能独特的低F(h)结构，而Standard保留高重要性的高F(h)结构，这种组成差异在SFT和GRPO训练中产生了完全不同的恢复轨迹。\n\n现在看GSM8K的post-prune数据，RASP在20%稀疏度下达到31.0%准确率，Standard只有27.0%，两者的95%置信区间刚好不重叠，确认了4个百分点的统计显著差异。这个结果与之前29倍的claim相差很大，但Recovery Amplification的叙事并不依赖post-prune的大差距——关键在于GRPO对这两种不同结构组成的差异化响应能力。\n\n接下来看SFT warmup恢复的实验，预期RASP在SFT后能达到57%的准确率，Standard达到64%，分别获得26和37个百分点的增益，两者的EOS率都是99%，最终训练损失都收敛到0.64。\n\n实验结果验证了这些预期，SFT成功修复了两个模型的格式问题。有趣的是Standard的SFT性能（64%）超过了RASP（57%），相差7个百分点，这看似反直觉但实际上支持了我的第三个假设——SFT通过模仿学习来扩展正确的推理路径，而Standard保留的高重叠结构为这种学习提供了更丰富的模板，尽管RASP的独特结构对强化学习更有利，但在模仿学习中的利用效率略低。\n\n两个模型的训练损失都收敛到0.64，token准确率都达到83%，说明学习过程充分。现在看一下具体的性能对比数据和损失曲线的表现。\n\nSFT预热阶段确立了关键前提：Standard方法在这个阶段优于RASP，这为后续的排名反转奠定了基础。接下来GRPO阶段需要验证这个反转是否真的发生。\n\n现在我看到GRPO训练后的具体性能指标——RASP在GSM8K上达到0.70，而Standard跌至0.53，这个17个百分点的恢复差距正是Recovery Amplification假说的核心证据。RASP的恢复率达到84.1%，而Standard只有63.7%，同时RASP的奖励信号和KL散度也显示出更健康的训练动态。\n\n关键在于RASP保留的低重叠MLP结构在GRPO的强化学习过程中充当了探索锚点，使得模型能够有效地重新分配被剪掉的高重叠结构的功能。\n\n而Standard模型虽然在SFT阶段因为高重叠结构提供了丰富的模仿模板而表现较好，但这些结构本身缺乏功能多样性，导致GRPO的探索无法在同质化的结构空间中找到有奖励的新路径，最终被KL惩罚侵蚀而性能下降。\n\n现在看到这种效应被放大了——post-prune的4pp差距在GRPO后扩大到17pp，说明GRPO作为非线性过程对结构组成的依赖远强于SFT。\n\n关键发现是排序反转：SFT阶段Standard表现更好（64% vs 57%），但GRPO后RASP大幅领先（70% vs 53%），而Standard在GRPO中反而下降11pp，这是最令人瞩目的——GRPO不仅没有帮助Standard，反而对其造成了伤害。现在准备在完整的GSM8K评估集上验证这些恢复模型的表现。 现在我在验证这些bootstrap结果的统计意义——RASP和Standard的置信区间完全不重叠，Cohen's h=0.35表示中等偏大的效应量，17个百分点的恢复差异在压缩模型上是实质性的改进。这10000次迭代的非参数置信界为这些发现提供了稳健的统计支持，我要把这些数据直接填入Table 1的\"+SFT+GRPO\"列。\n\nGenerating markdown table... 57, 70, 84.1, \"[67.4, 72.4]\"]\n          - [Standard, 27.0, 64, 53, 63.7, \"[50.3, 55.7]\"]\n          - [\"GRASPrune†\", 10, 35, 38, 45.7, \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart：所有方法在每个pipeline阶段的accuracy。箭头标注recovery magnitude。Figure 1 of paper。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Table 1是paper的锚定结果。叙事清晰：相同模型、相同稀疏度、相同recovery预算——\n      唯一区别是pruning criterion。RASP的CKA-awareness将recovery rate从64%提升到\n      84.1%，提升20个百分点。\n\nNow I'm setting up the GRASPrune baseline experiment at 20% sparsity, which is the main external comparison point. This includes the full pipeline from gate training through pruning, evaluation, and then SFT with GRPO optimization, with expected performance metrics showing how much recovery is possible with their approach.\n\nLooking at the actual results, GRASPrune's post-pruning accuracy is only 10%, which is surprisingly low compared to the Standard baseline at 27%. This is counterintuitive since GRASPrune's learned gates should theoretically outperform static importance scoring. The key insight is that GRASPrune optimizes gates based on reconstruction loss and perplexity, which prioritizes what's important for language modeling rather than what matters for reasoning tasks—so for a distilled reasoning model, the structures that preserve perplexity aren't necessarily the same ones needed for chain-of-thought reasoning.\n\nWhat's interesting is the recovery pattern: GRASPrune bounces back from 10% to 38% with GRPO training (+28pp gain), while Standard goes from 27% to 53% (+26pp). Even though GRASPrune starts much lower, it actually recovers slightly more aggressively than Standard. This breaks the assumption that recovery is just a linear function of post-pruning accuracy. The gates that seemed suboptimal initially actually preserved enough functional redundancy through implicit gradient flow that GRPO has room to redistribute and recover. RASP shows even stronger recovery gains at +39pp, suggesting a different mechanism entirely.\n\nNow I'm looking at the performance metrics across the pipeline stages for all three methods, and I can see GRASPrune positioned in the middle during recovery. The scatter plot shows how post-pruning accuracy relates to GRPO recovery gains, and the three methods clearly don't follow a simple linear relationship.\n\nGRASPrune serves as a crucial middle baseline that isolates two key confounds: RASP's advantage isn't simply from better importance estimation since GRASPrune also has learned gates but underperforms, and recovery gains aren't just a function of post-pruning accuracy—GRASPrune jumps from 10% to 38% (28 percentage points) while Standard only gains 26 percentage points despite starting from 27%. This shows CKA is the critical missing piece for optimal recovery during pruning.\n\nI'm also planning a multi-seed evaluation across five different random seeds to validate the RASP and Standard pruning results at 20% sparsity. 验证post-prune gap的统计稳健性。跨5个seed的结果显示RASP和Standard模型的性能差异稳定一致，均值差为4.5个百分点，标准差仅0.8pp。配对t检验的p值为0.0002，强烈证实这是系统性差异而非随机波动，两个模型的calibration稳定性都很高。\n\n剪枝决策的跨seed重叠率在87-93%之间，说明核心的剪枝选择是稳定的，只有少数边界情况会随calibration变化。\n\nGenerating robustness table... The paired t-test shows highly significant results at p=0.0002, and even though the post-pruning gap is modest at 4.5 percentage points, it's statistically robust when combined with the larger N=1319 evaluation from plan_001—this gives strong evidence for Claim 1's post-pruning component. Now I'm looking at a scoring ablation study at 20% sparsity that isolates different components of the RASP scoring function: full RASP, CKA-only, gradient-only, magnitude-only, and random baselines to understand each component's contribution.\n\nThe results show a clear hierarchy across methods—RASP full at 31%, CKA-only at 29%, gradient-only at 27%, magnitude-only at 25%, and random at 18%—but the differences between CKA and gradient-only are small with overlapping confidence intervals, suggesting CKA's marginal benefit at the post-pruning stage is limited, which is actually revealing something important about the recovery amplification mechanism.\n\nThe real insight is that while structured scoring methods consistently outperform random selection by a meaningful margin, the differences between importance-based approaches are much smaller at this stage. Importance-based methods contribute about 9 percentage points over random, whereas CKA's additional contribution over gradient-only is only 2 percentage points, but this relationship reverses after recovery when GRPO amplifies CKA's effect—meaning the two components work synergistically rather than independently. Now I'm looking at the ablation results across different scoring methods—the horizontal bar chart will show how RASP's combination of information content and CKA alignment outperforms the individual components, with the post-pruning differences being relatively modest compared to the larger gains we see during the GRPO training phase. I'm also planning a mixed-effects regression analysis at the MLP channel group level to examine how CKA-recoverability correlates with structural properties across the 784 groups in the model.\n\nExamining the regression metrics...\n\nThe mixed-effects model confirms CKA overlap as a strong predictor of recoverability in MLP channel groups—the standardized coefficient of 0.38 with p-value of 0.00034 remains significant even after controlling for weight norm, gradient importance, and activation magnitude. The partial R² of 0.22 shows CKA independently accounts for about a fifth of the recoverability variance, which makes sense because CKA directly captures functional redundancy—how much one group's computation is duplicated by others in the same layer.\n\nThis is fundamentally a proxy for whether GRPO can redistribute a pruned group's functionality to the remaining groups. While weight norm, gradient importance, and activation magnitude measure how critical a group currently is, they don't capture whether other groups can actually take over its role if it's removed. The intraclass correlation of 0.18 reveals moderate clustering across layers, with the strongest CKA-recoverability coupling in middle layers (8-18) where redistribution primarily occurs, while early and late layers show weaker effects. The conditional R² of 0.49 versus marginal R² of 0.31 indicates layer effects explain an additional 18% of variance, and the diagnostic metrics look clean with variance inflation factors below 3.\n\nGenerating regression table... Looking at the figures I'm planning to create: a scatter plot showing the relationship between F(h) and recoverability with layer-based coloring and prediction bands, a coefficient plot displaying the 95% confidence intervals for the four predictors where CKA clearly separates from zero while others hover near it, and a caterpillar plot of the random effects across all 28 layers showing that middle layers have the highest intercepts. The analysis confirms that CKA is the dominant predictor at 3.2 times stronger than the next best (gradient), uniquely explaining 22% of the variance and validating that the RASP framework captures recoverability signals that standard metrics miss, with layer-specific random effects revealing structural patterns in how different depths contribute to this relationship.\n\nNow I'm setting up a comparison experiment where I apply only SFT recovery to the same pruned models with the same data budget, without GRPO, to create a 2×2 interaction analysis alongside the main results. I'm projecting specific performance metrics and confidence intervals for this SFT-only condition across both RASP and standard approaches. Looking at the performance metrics, there's a striking ranking reversal: Standard dominates under SFT-only (66% vs 58%), but RASP flips to lead under SFT+GRPO (70% vs 53%), creating a 25 percentage point interaction effect that's highly significant. The mechanism appears to be that SFT's imitation learning reinforces high-overlap structures where Standard excels, but GRPO's reinforcement learning allows RASP's sparser architecture to leverage multiple solution pathways more effectively.\n\nGenerating comparison table... The interaction effect with p=0.0008 strongly supports the claim. What's compelling here is that neither pruning nor recovery method shows a significant main effect on their own—RASP and Standard perform similarly on average, as do SFT and GRPO—but the interaction between them is massive at 25 percentage points, meaning the optimal pruning strategy fundamentally depends on which recovery method you're using.\n\nNow I'm looking at the expected results for the 25% sparsity experiment across the full pipeline, tracking how RASP maintains an 8 percentage point advantage right after pruning and then achieves a 23 percentage point recovery gap after both SFT and GRPO, compared to Standard's much smaller recovery rate. Generating comparison table... At 30% sparsity, I'm running just pruning and evaluation without recovery to identify where each method hits its collapse threshold. RASP drops to 8% accuracy while Standard falls to 3%, confirming that RASP maintains some inference capability but enters the collapse zone—consistent with the complete failure we see at 35% sparsity. This establishes the upper bound of recoverable sparsity for the DeepSeek-R1-Distill model.\n\nLooking at the broader pattern, RASP's effective operating range is around 25%, with 30% marking the boundary and 35%+ showing complete collapse. Standard method hits its limit much earlier at 20%, and even at 27% sparsity it only recovers to 53% accuracy. Skipping recovery at this point is the right call since the 8% post-prune accuracy would produce such sparse reward signals that GRPO training likely wouldn't converge—the model needs sufficient baseline performance to discover rewarded paths.\n\nGenerating sparsity collapse map... Now I'm setting up the out-of-distribution evaluation across MATH-500 and HumanEval benchmarks, comparing the best recovered configurations from both RASP and Standard approaches against the baseline to see how well the recovery generalizes beyond GSM8K. The retention rates across benchmarks are remarkably consistent—RASP maintains around 80% performance while standard pruning drops to roughly 60-66%—suggesting that RASP preserves a general reasoning scaffold rather than patterns specific to any single benchmark. This consistency strengthens the argument that RASP's advantages generalize across different task types. Now I'm compiling the cross-benchmark evaluation table with the performance metrics... Looking at the Bonsai baseline results, the activation-based importance scoring gives a slightly lower post-prune performance of 24% compared to Standard's 27%, but SFT recovery brings it to 50%. The interesting pattern is that GRPO actually hurts Bonsai's performance by 3 percentage points, mirroring what we saw with Standard—suggesting this negative effect isn't unique to one pruning method but rather a broader issue with how GRPO interacts with the pruned models.\n\nGenerating comparison table... Looking at the reliability metrics, the split-half Spearman correlation of 0.93 confirms that the CKA scoring function is highly consistent across independent calibration samples. The linear CKA approach has already converged by 512 samples—the rank correlation between 256 and 512 samples drops to 0.90, suggesting diminishing returns from additional calibration data, while the 512 to 1024 comparison shows much stronger agreement at 0.97.\n\nThe downstream task performance barely changes with larger calibration sets: moving from 256 to 512 samples improves GSM8K accuracy by 2 percentage points, and 512 to 1024 adds only 1 more point, well within the inter-seed variance range. The pruned set overlap remains stable at 86-95% across different calibration sizes, indicating that the core pruning decisions are robust to this choice. This validation work is crucial for establishing the credibility of the approach.\n\nGenerating metrics table...\n\nThe split-half consistency check shows strong reliability at ρ=0.93, and rank stability between calibration sizes is excellent, particularly the 0.97 correlation between 512 and 1024 configurations. This analysis belongs in the appendix with just a brief mention in the main text referencing the split-half consistency result.\n\nNow I'm examining the sensitivity of the α parameter across different values to understand how the weighting factor affects pruning performance at 20% sparsity. S(h)=I(h)×(1-F(h))^α的唯一自由参数分析。预期结果显示α在不同值下的性能：α=0时GSM8K达25%，α=2.0时达35%，最优α为2.0，相比α=0提升10个百分点，曲线呈单调递增且收益递减的形态。\n\n当使用推理轨迹校准来计算importance时，虽然CoT traces的长度和噪声导致importance估计略低于标准困惑度校准，但CKA组件有效补偿了这个差距。从α=0的25%到α=2.0的35%，性能持续提升，其中α=0.5已超过标准的27%达到29%。增量分析显示α=0到0.5增加4个百分点，0.5到1.0增加2个百分点，1.0到2.0又增加4个百分点，高α值处的加速趋势表明最优点可能在α>2.0，这与之前α=4.0达到40%的预实验结果一致。\n\n从实践角度看，α是RASP中唯一需要调整的参数，这个消融实验为使用者提供了明确的调参指导——α=1是合理的默认值，但α=2可能更优，虽然需要更多验证。这10个百分点的改进量化了CKA作为剪枝信号的价值，在相同的importance框架下，添加CKA重叠加权能将修剪后的准确率提升10个百分点。\n\nGenerating markdown table... Looking at the inference speedup benchmark, I'm comparing wall-clock latency and throughput across the dense baseline, RASP with 20% sparsity, and Standard with 20% sparsity—both structured pruning approaches achieve roughly 28-29% speedup over dense while maintaining similar latency profiles, validating the practical efficiency gains. memory_reduction_percent: 18.5\nresult_rationale: >\n20%结构化稀疏度提供1.28x推理加速（12.4→9.7 ms/token），因为移除的200个MLP channel groups直接减少了矩阵维度，不需要sparse hardware支持。RASP和Standard的speedup几乎相同（1.28 vs 1.29），因为两者移除了相同数量的结构（200个MLP groups），只是选择了不同的groups。微小差异来自不同groups的memory access pattern差异。Memory减少18.5%（略低于20%因为有些参数如embedding不参与剪枝）。这1.28x的加速在实际应用中很显著：batch serving时可以在同一GPU上多处理约28%的tokens，或者单个查询的延迟从100ms降到78ms。与非结构化剪枝对比特别重要——20%的非结构化剪枝几乎没有加速效果（需要sparse tensor cores支持），而结构化RASP方法提供了真实可用的1.28x加速。现在看一下推理基准的具体数据。\n\nGenerating benchmark table... Now I'm setting up the baseline for unstructured pruning at 20% sparsity to establish the gap between structured and unstructured approaches. The unstructured method preserves all architectural components but removes individual weights uniformly, which explains why it maintains much higher post-pruning accuracy compared to structured methods.\n\nThe recovery trajectory is interesting though—unstructured starts higher at 45% versus RASP's 31%, but after SFT and GRPO reaches only 60% compared to RASP's 70%. This happens because uniform weight removal across all structures leaves GRPO without clear \"donor\" and \"receiver\" patterns that structured pruning creates, making the redistribution mechanism less effective at recovering lost capabilities. GRPO能够清晰地将donor的功能重新分配给receiver。关键对比是unstructured只达到1.02倍加速，而RASP结构化剪枝在准确率（70% vs 60%）和推理速度（1.28倍 vs 1.02倍）两个维度都更优。从散点图来看，RASP结构化方案位于右上角（高准确率+高加速），而unstructured则在左下角，这充分论证了为什么结构化剪枝更有优势。现在我需要检查SFT恢复模型在OOD评估上的表现。 The key finding is that Standard SFT's sharp drop from 64% on GSM8K to 35% on MATH-500 (54% retention) versus RASP's more modest drop from 57% to 42% (72% retention) reveals that Standard's high GSM8K accuracy relied heavily on memorizing dataset-specific solution patterns rather than developing generalizable reasoning—these fixed templates don't transfer to the diverse mathematical problems in MATH-500, whereas RASP's approach, despite lower absolute performance on GSM8K, demonstrates much stronger generalization across different problem distributions.\n\nGenerating markdown table...\n\nNow I'm double-checking the ANOVA results from the interaction analysis—the pruning main effect of 4.5 percentage points with p=0.11 looks right, confirming that while there's a directional effect, it doesn't reach statistical significance.\n\nFor the MATH-500 baseline, I should use reasonable estimates aligned with known model performance rather than assuming specific values. And for the speedup calculation from 20% structured pruning, the theoretical speedup works out to roughly 1.15x when accounting for MLPs representing about two-thirds of the computational load in transformer layers.\n\nActually, 1.28x seems defensible when I factor in memory bandwidth improvements and cache efficiency gains—modern GPUs are often memory-bound during inference, so removing 20% of MLP channels proportionally reduces memory traffic and improves cache behavior, pushing the actual speedup closer to 1.25-1.28x.\n\nFor plan_010's 25% sparsity, I need to be more precise about the structure count: with 784 MLP groups and 112 attention GQA groups totaling around 900 structures, a 25% sparsity level would affect roughly 225 of those structures.\n\nNow I'm checking plan_009's performance metrics against the best-tier ranges—my sft_only values need to fall within the specified bounds for both the RASP and standard variants.\n\nFor the statistical analysis, I'm setting up a 2×2 factorial design with binary outcomes across the four conditions: RASP with SFT-only, RASP with SFT+GRPO, standard with SFT-only, and standard with SFT+GRPO. With N=1319 samples per cell, I should use logistic regression rather than ANOVA to properly model the binary nature of the outcomes.\n\nThe interaction effect between the model type and training approach would be highly significant given these sample sizes—the 25 percentage point difference in how RASP and standard models respond to GRPO training is substantial enough that p<0.0001 is realistic, though I'll keep it at p=0.0008 to reflect a strong but not extreme result. The metric just requires the interaction to be significant (p<0.05), so this works well.\n\nNow I'm reconsidering the statistical approach for this comparison. Since we're evaluating four different model configurations on the same test set, a paired analysis like McNemar's test or GEE would be more appropriate than a standard ANOVA, but for the YAML output I'll just report the interaction p-value without specifying the exact test used.\n\nI need to think through the SFT-only baseline more carefully—the key constraint is that it uses the same data budget as the SFT+GRPO condition, which means if GRPO gets some portion of the total training compute, the SFT-only model would use that entire budget for additional SFT iterations instead. FT-only gets 10 GPU-hours of SFT. The SFT warmup (plan_002) used ~1.2 GPU-hours (37 min × 2 GPUs). So the extended SFT in plan_009 would be ~5x longer.\n\nWith 5x more SFT training:\n- RASP: might improve from 57% to 58-59%\n- Standard: might improve from 64% to 65-66%\n\nSFT saturates quickly, so extended training gives diminishing returns. Setting RASP=58% and Standard=66% seems reasonable.\n\nWhether \"same data budget\" means GPU-hours or number of training examples, the math works out similarly—SFT-only would still see ~24000 total samples across epochs, which is already saturated territory.\n\nNow I'm noticing a key issue with the recovery amplification narrative: Standard drops from 64% after SFT warmup to 53% after GRPO, which is an 11-point decline. For plan_009, I need to clarify what the actual comparison points are.\n\nThe GRPO in plan_003 is applied on top of the warmup SFT baseline (64%), not the extended SFT (66%). So the GRPO marginal effect is -11pp relative to warmup. But when comparing plan_009 (extended SFT-only at 66%) to plan_003 (SFT+GRPO at 53%), the difference is -13pp. The issue is that these aren't directly comparable since the SFT-only path got more training, so I need to be careful about how I frame this comparison.\n\nFor a fair interaction test at the same compute budget, I'm looking at RASP versus Standard across both SFT-only and SFT+GRPO conditions. RASP shows a +12pp gain from GRPO while Standard shows a -13pp loss, giving an interaction effect of 25pp between the two approaches.\n\nNow I'm ready to write out the final YAML with the results, keeping the explanations concise given how much content needs to be covered.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6569,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39107,"cache_read_input_tokens":29475,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39107},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5a2ac1e-eb55-43b9-94d1-02900c2c612b","uuid":"bb000fc5-0f18-44c0-935b-fa70e313e6f4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AkU55iE1LxBag1bRQRELGw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a complete picture of the project state, the existing dream report, actual experimental results, and the best-tier definition. Key calibration points from actual data:\n- reeval_postprune_definitive: RASP=31%, Standard=27% (4pp gap, not 28pp)\n- SFT: RASP=57%, Standard=64% (Standard higher)\n- GRASPrune preliminary: 8% (50 samples)\n- α=4.0 gave 40% post-prune\n\nGenerating the best-tier predictions calibrated to the Recovery Amplification narrative.\n\n```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Recovery Amplification版本：post-prune差异仅4-8pp（31% vs 27%），但GRPO将其\n  放大为17pp recovery gap（70% vs 53%）。更关键的是ranking reversal：SFT下\n  Standard>RASP（66%>58%），GRPO后RASP>>Standard（70%>>53%）。Redundancy Paradox\n  的表现形式不是post-prune的绝对优势，而是GRPO对不同结构组成的差异化响应——\n  GRPO对RASP +12pp，对Standard -13pp。三个claims全部成立：Claim 1修正为\n  \"recovery amplification\"而非\"29x advantage\"；Claim 2的CKA correlation在MLP\n  groups上显著（partial R²=0.22）；Claim 3的排序反转完整成立。GRASPrune打破\n  \"recovery只反映post-prune accuracy\"的线性假设。α ablation给出10pp的CKA贡献\n  量化。OOD eval确认泛化。竞争力：EMNLP Main强投稿，Efficient Methods track。\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K Evaluation (N=1319)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"N=1319全集评估baseline + RASP_20 + Standard_20，替换N=100快速评估，产出publication-quality CI。\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_gsm8k_1319: 0.832\n      baseline_ci95: [0.811, 0.852]\n      rasp_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.31\n      rasp_20_ci95: [0.286, 0.335]\n      standard_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.27\n      standard_20_ci95: [0.246, 0.295]\n      rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 4\n      mcnemar_p: 0.0038\n      rasp_retention_rate: 0.373\n      standard_retention_rate: 0.324\n    result_rationale: >\n      Full N=1319确认reeval_postprune_definitive：RASP 31%、Standard 27%，gap仅4pp。\n      CI从±9pp（N=100）收窄到±2.5pp，McNemar在N=1319下显著（p=0.004）。Baseline\n      83.2%符合DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B的已知GSM8K population accuracy。4pp的\n      post-prune差异表明两种方法保留了相似总量的推理能力，但结构组成不同：RASP保留\n      功能独特的MLP groups（低F(h)锚点），Standard保留高importance的MLP groups（往\n      往高F(h)、高重叠）。这种组成差异在post-prune层面效果有限（4pp），但在GRPO\n      recovery阶段被非线性放大——因为GRPO的redistribution机制对结构多样性的依赖\n      远强于SFT的imitation learning。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Post-Prune GSM8K (N=1319)\"\n        columns: [Method, Sparsity, \"Acc (%)\", \"95% CI\", \"Retention (%)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Baseline, \"0%\", 83.2, \"[81.1, 85.2]\", \"—\"]\n          - [RASP, \"20%\", 31.0, \"[28.6, 33.5]\", 37.3]\n          - [Standard, \"20%\", 27.0, \"[24.6, 29.5]\", 32.4]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"柱状图+95% CI，三个条件。Y轴GSM8K accuracy。4pp gap的CI边缘不重叠。\"\n    analysis: >\n      N=1319确认post-prune gap为4pp且显著。这是Recovery Amplification叙事的起点：\n      小的post-prune差异经过GRPO放大后变成不可逆的recovery gap。\n\n  - name: \"SFT Warmup Recovery\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"RASP_20和Standard_20的SFT warmup恢复。[DONE — 使用实际结果]\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_post_sft: 0.57\n      standard_20_post_sft: 0.64\n      rasp_sft_gain_pp: 26\n      standard_sft_gain_pp: 37\n      rasp_eos_rate: 0.99\n      standard_eos_rate: 0.99\n      rasp_train_loss_final: 0.64\n      standard_train_loss_final: 0.64\n    result_rationale: >\n      [实际结果] Standard SFT(64%) > RASP SFT(57%)，差7pp。SFT通过模仿学习\n      \"扩展\"正确路径（\"SFT Expands\"），偏好高重叠结构——这正是Standard保留的结构\n      类型。Standard的高重叠MLP groups参与多条推理路径，提供了丰富的solution\n      templates供SFT模仿利用。RASP保留的功能独特结构虽然对GRPO redistribution更\n      有利，但在SFT的imitation paradigm下利用效率较低。两者train loss均收敛到0.64、\n      EOS rate 99%，说明SFT学习充分、差异来自结构组成而非训练不充分。Standard SFT\n      优势在N=100下CI重叠（ER-001），不作为Claim 3独立证据，但与GRPO联合构成交互效应。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Post-SFT Warmup\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Post-Prune (%)\", \"Post-SFT (%)\", \"SFT Gain (pp)\", \"EOS Rate\"]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP_20, 31, 57, +26, 0.99]\n          - [Standard_20, 27, 64, +37, 0.99]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"SFT loss曲线对比。两曲线近乎重合（均收敛到0.64），差异来自结构组成非训练动态。\"\n    analysis: >\n      SFT结果锚定了ranking reversal的\"before\"状态：SFT下Standard优于RASP。\n      GRPO（plan_003）需要将此反转。\n\n  - name: \"GRPO Recovery on SFT-Warmed Models\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"GRPO Stage 2恢复。RASP和Standard均从SFT-warmed模型开始，相同超参数和计算预算。核心MVP实验。\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_post_grpo_gsm8k: 0.70\n      rasp_post_grpo_ci95: [0.675, 0.724]\n      standard_post_grpo_gsm8k: 0.53\n      standard_post_grpo_ci95: [0.503, 0.557]\n      grpo_recovery_gap_pp: 17\n      rasp_grpo_gain_over_sft_pp: 13\n      standard_grpo_gain_over_sft_pp: -11\n      rasp_recovery_rate: 0.841\n      standard_recovery_rate: 0.637\n      rasp_reward_mean_final: 0.62\n      standard_reward_mean_final: 0.45\n      rasp_kl_final: 4.1\n      standard_kl_final: 1.8\n      amplification_factor: 4.25\n    result_rationale: >\n      GRPO是Recovery Amplification的核心。RASP 57%→70%（+13pp）：RASP保留的功能\n      独特MLP groups充当GRPO exploration的锚点，编码不可替代的推理子步骤。GRPO通过\n      \"RL Squeezes\"将被剪掉的高重叠groups的功能重新分配到这些锚点。reward从~0.3\n      稳步上升到0.62，KL=4.1表示显著policy移动——模型在积极探索并找到压缩后的推理路径。\n      Standard 64%→53%（-11pp）：GRPO反而伤害了Standard。Standard的高重叠结构为\n      SFT提供了丰富模仿模板（故SFT达64%），但缺乏功能多样性——GRPO exploration在\n      同质化结构空间中找不到有奖励的新路径。KL penalty逐步侵蚀SFT学到的脆弱表面\n      模式，exploration无法补偿损失。reward在0.45震荡（能部分答对但无法持续提升）。\n      核心数字：4pp post-prune gap → 17pp post-GRPO gap，amplification 4.25x。\n      这证明GRPO是非线性过程，对结构组成的依赖远强于SFT。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"SFT→GRPO Recovery Pipeline\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Post-Prune (%)\", \"Post-SFT (%)\", \"Post-GRPO (%)\", \"GRPO Δ (pp)\", \"Recovery (%)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP_20, 31, 57, 70, +13, 84.1]\n          - [Standard_20, 27, 64, 53, -11, 63.7]\n          - [Baseline, 83.2, \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"GRPO reward曲线：RASP稳步上升到0.62，Standard在0.45震荡。\"\n      - \"Waterfall：post-prune→post-SFT→post-GRPO，RASP持续恢复vs Standard的GRPO退化。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Headline result。Ranking reversal完成：SFT下Standard>RASP (64>57)，GRPO后\n      RASP>>Standard (70>>53)。Standard的-11pp GRPO drop是最引人注目的发现——\n      GRPO不仅未帮助Standard，反而主动伤害它。Recovery Amplification confirmed。\n\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K Eval on Recovered Models (N=1319)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"N=1319 bootstrap CI评估所有recovered模型，产出Table 1最终数据。\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_recovered_1319: 0.70\n      rasp_ci95_bootstrap: [0.674, 0.724]\n      standard_recovered_1319: 0.53\n      standard_ci95_bootstrap: [0.503, 0.557]\n      gap_pp: 17\n      cohens_h: 0.35\n      bootstrap_iterations: 10000\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bootstrap CI确认17pp gap统计稳健，CI不重叠。Cohen's h=0.35为中等偏大效应量——\n      不是原始framing的\"巨大\"效应，但17pp在compressed model上是实质性差异（从\n      Standard的勉强可用到RASP的接近baseline性能）。这些数据填入Table 1 \"+SFT+GRPO\"列。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Main Results at 20% Structured Sparsity\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Post-Prune (%)\", \"Post-SFT (%)\", \"Post-SFT+GRPO (%)\", \"Recovery (%)\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Baseline, 83.2, \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"[81.1, 85.2]\"]\n          - [RASP, 31, 57, 70, 84.1, \"[67.4, 72.4]\"]\n          - [Standard, 27, 64, 53, 63.7, \"[50.3, 55.7]\"]\n          - [\"GRASPrune†\", 10, 35, 38, 45.7, \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart：pipeline各阶段accuracy。Paper Figure 1。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Table 1锚定全文。同sparsity、同recovery budget，唯一区别是pruning criterion——\n      RASP的CKA-awareness将recovery rate从64%提升到84%（+20pp）。\n\n  - name: \"GRASPrune Baseline at 20% Sparsity\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"GRASPrune（ACL 2026 SOTA budgeted pruning）完整pipeline。排除recovery-只-反映-post-prune-accuracy的混淆。\"\n    expected_results:\n      grasp_post_prune_gsm8k: 0.10\n      grasp_post_prune_ci95: [0.084, 0.118]\n      grasp_post_sft_gsm8k: 0.35\n      grasp_post_grpo_gsm8k: 0.38\n      grasp_post_grpo_ci95: [0.354, 0.407]\n      grasp_recovery_rate: 0.457\n      grasp_grpo_gain_pp: 3\n      grasp_vs_rasp_recovered_gap_pp: -32\n    result_rationale: >\n      GRASPrune post-prune仅10%（与预实验8%/50样本一致），远低于Standard 27%。这出\n      人意料：GRASPrune的learned gates理论上应优于static Taylor。原因：gates通过\n      reconstruction loss训练，优化\"对语言建模最重要的结构\"而非\"对推理链最重要的\n      结构\"——perplexity-optimal和reasoning-optimal存在系统偏差。\n      关键发现在recovery pattern：GRASPrune 10%→38%（+28pp GRPO gain），Standard\n      27%→53%（+26pp）。GRASPrune起点远低于Standard（-17pp），但GRPO增量略高\n      （+28>+26）。这打破了\"recovery只是post-prune accuracy函数\"的线性假设：如果\n      recovery仅反映post-prune accuracy，GRASPrune应该恢复更少。GRASPrune gates\n      通过梯度流隐式保留了部分功能冗余结构，给GRPO一定redistribution空间，尽管\n      immediate accuracy很差。RASP（+39pp gain，31→70%）远超两者——显式CKA优化\n      比隐式捕获有效得多。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"GRASPrune Pipeline\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Post-Prune (%)\", \"Post-SFT (%)\", \"Post-GRPO (%)\", \"GRPO Gain (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP, 31, 57, 70, +13]\n          - [Standard, 27, 64, 53, -11]\n          - [GRASPrune, 10, 35, 38, +3]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三方法pipeline柱状图。\"\n      - \"Scatter: post-prune accuracy (x) vs GRPO gain (y)，三个点打破线性。\"\n    analysis: >\n      GRASPrune排除两个混淆：(1) RASP优势≠更好的importance estimation（GRASPrune\n      has learned gates yet worse）；(2) recovery≠post-prune accuracy的简单函数。\n      CKA是recovery-optimal pruning的missing ingredient。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-Seed Post-Prune Evaluation (5 Seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"5种子（42,123,7,256,1337）RASP和Standard 20%剪枝+N=1319评估。Post-prune gap的统计稳健性验证。\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_seeds: {42: 0.310, 123: 0.302, 7: 0.321, 256: 0.298, 1337: 0.324}\n      rasp_mean: 0.311\n      rasp_std: 0.011\n      standard_seeds: {42: 0.270, 123: 0.258, 7: 0.275, 256: 0.261, 1337: 0.266}\n      standard_mean: 0.266\n      standard_std: 0.007\n      paired_diffs: [0.040, 0.044, 0.046, 0.037, 0.058]\n      mean_gap_pp: 4.5\n      gap_std_pp: 0.8\n      paired_t_p: 0.0002\n      pruned_set_overlap_range: [0.87, 0.93]\n    result_rationale: >\n      5-seed paired t-test p=0.0002确认4.5pp gap是系统性差异。RASP σ=1.1pp，\n      Standard σ=0.7pp——CKA和Taylor importance在512 calibration样本上已充分收敛。\n      所有5个seed的差异均为正（3.7-5.8pp），无reversal。Pruned set overlap 87-93%\n      表明~180/200 MLP groups跨seed一致，仅14-26个边界groups随calibration变化。\n      稳定性来源：linear CKA是kernel-based statistic，512个mean-pooled activations\n      提供>400有效数据点，远超stable estimation threshold。这排除了\"lucky seed\"和\n      \"calibration artifact\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"5-Seed Robustness\"\n        columns: [Seed, \"RASP (%)\", \"Standard (%)\", \"Gap (pp)\", \"Pruned Set Overlap (%)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [42, 31.0, 27.0, 4.0, \"—\"]\n          - [123, 30.2, 25.8, 4.4, 93]\n          - [7, 32.1, 27.5, 4.6, 89]\n          - [256, 29.8, 26.1, 3.7, 91]\n          - [1337, 32.4, 26.6, 5.8, 87]\n          - [\"Mean±Std\", \"31.1±1.1\", \"26.6±0.7\", \"4.5±0.8\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired strip plot，5 seeds连线。所有连线斜率为正。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Post-prune gap虽小（4.5pp），但5-seed p=0.0002稳健。Claim 1的post-prune\n      component有充分统计支持。\n\n  - name: \"Scoring Ablation at 20% Sparsity\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"RASP评分函数控制消融：magnitude-only, gradient-only, random, CKA-only。隔离各组件贡献。\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_full_gsm8k: 0.31\n      cka_only_gsm8k: 0.29\n      gradient_only_gsm8k: 0.27\n      magnitude_only_gsm8k: 0.25\n      random_gsm8k: 0.18\n    result_rationale: >\n      Post-prune差异较小但系统性：RASP(31%)>CKA-only(29%)>gradient(27%,=Standard)>\n      magnitude(25%)>random(18%)。CKA-only vs gradient仅差2pp，CI部分重叠——在\n      post-prune层面CKA的边际贡献有限。但这恰恰是Recovery Amplification要点：\n      post-prune差异小，GRPO放大差异。Importance贡献（gradient 27% vs random 18%=\n      9pp）在post-prune层面实际上大于CKA边际贡献（CKA-only 29% vs gradient 27%=2pp）。\n      但这个关系在recovery后反转：CKA-aware结构的GRPO recoverability远高于\n      importance-only结构。Random at 18%确认structured scoring确实优于随机。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Scoring Ablation (Post-Prune)\"\n        columns: [Scoring, Formula, \"GSM8K (%)\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP (full)\", \"I(h)×(1-F(h))^α\", 31.0, \"[28.6, 33.5]\"]\n          - [\"CKA-only\", \"(1-F(h))^α\", 29.0, \"[26.6, 31.5]\"]\n          - [\"Gradient-only (=Std)\", \"I(h)\", 27.0, \"[24.6, 29.5]\"]\n          - [\"Magnitude-only\", \"||w_h||₂\", 25.0, \"[22.6, 27.5]\"]\n          - [\"Random\", \"Uniform\", 18.0, \"[15.9, 20.3]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"水平柱状图按accuracy排序。标注Standard baseline reference line (27%)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Post-prune ablation提供组件归因。差异较小但结构清晰。需与recovery数据联合\n      解读——真正的区分在GRPO阶段。\n\n  - name: \"Per-Structure CKA-Recoverability Correlation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"MLP channel group级mixed-effects回归。N=784 MLP groups，layer random effect。控制weight norm/gradient/activation。\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_mlp_groups: 784\n      n_pruned: 200\n      n_layers: 28\n      cka_beta: 0.38\n      cka_se: 0.055\n      cka_t: 6.91\n      cka_p: 0.00034\n      cka_partial_r2: 0.22\n      gradient_beta: 0.12\n      gradient_p: 0.019\n      weight_norm_beta: 0.07\n      weight_norm_p: 0.15\n      activation_beta: 0.04\n      activation_p: 0.42\n      marginal_r2: 0.31\n      conditional_r2: 0.49\n      icc_layer: 0.18\n      vif_max: 2.6\n    result_rationale: >\n      CKA β=0.38 (p=0.0003)在控制weight norm(n.s.)、gradient(marginal p=0.019)、\n      activation(n.s.)后仍显著dominant，partial R²=0.22独立解释22%方差。这是因为\n      CKA overlap直接度量functional redundancy——\"这个MLP group的计算被同层其他\n      groups复制的程度\"——本质上就是\"GRPO能否将被剪group的功能重新分配给剩余groups\"\n      的代理指标。Weight/gradient/activation度量\"当前有多重要\"，不度量\"功能能否\n      被接管\"。ICC=0.18表明层间存在中等聚类：middle layers(8-18)的CKA-recoverability\n      耦合最强（推理redistribution集中于此），与\"RL Squeezes\"机制一致。\n      注意：分析仅在MLP groups(N=784)上进行，20%稀疏度下0/112 attention GQA groups\n      被剪——CKA信号的实际效果是在MLP groups间做reranking。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Mixed-Effects Regression\"\n        columns: [Predictor, \"β (std)\", SE, p, \"Partial R²\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"F(h) CKA overlap\", 0.38, 0.055, \"<0.001\", 0.22]\n          - [\"I(h) gradient\", 0.12, 0.052, 0.019, 0.04]\n          - [\"Weight norm\", 0.07, 0.050, 0.15, 0.01]\n          - [\"Activation mag.\", 0.04, 0.050, 0.42, \"<0.01\"]\n          - [\"Marginal R²\", 0.31, \"\", \"\", \"\"]\n          - [\"Conditional R²\", 0.49, \"\", \"\", \"\"]\n          - [\"ICC (layer)\", 0.18, \"\", \"\", \"\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: per-group F(h) vs recoverability，按layer depth着色，回归线+prediction band。\"\n      - \"Coefficient plot: 4 predictors的95% CI，CKA明确与零分离。\"\n      - \"Caterpillar plot: 28层random effects，middle layers intercept最高。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Claim 2核心证据。CKA(β=0.38)是next-best predictor(gradient β=0.12)的3.2倍，\n      独立解释22%方差。验证了RASP设计理论基础。\n\n  - name: \"SFT-Only Recovery Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"相同pruned模型、相同总计算预算，仅SFT恢复。与plan_003联合构成2×2交互分析，验证Claim 3。\"\n    expected_results:\n      sft_only_rasp: 0.58\n      sft_only_standard: 0.66\n      sft_grpo_rasp: 0.70\n      sft_grpo_standard: 0.53\n      grpo_marginal_rasp_pp: 12\n      grpo_marginal_standard_pp: -13\n      interaction_pp: 25\n      interaction_p: 0.0008\n      rasp_adv_under_sft_pp: -8\n      rasp_adv_under_grpo_pp: 17\n    result_rationale: >\n      Extended SFT（全预算）RASP=58%、Standard=66%，与warmup SFT接近（SFT饱和快）。\n      核心交互：\n      SFT-only: Standard(66%) > RASP(58%) → Standard wins by 8pp\n      SFT+GRPO: RASP(70%) > Standard(53%) → RASP wins by 17pp\n      → 完整ranking reversal。交互效应=12-(-13)=25pp, p=0.0008。\n      机制：\"SFT Expands\"偏好高重叠结构（Standard保留的），模仿学习在多条重叠路径\n      上同时强化。\"RL Squeezes\"需要功能独特锚点（RASP保留的），exploration要求\n      结构多样性来发现新推理路径。Standard缺乏这些锚点，GRPO的KL penalty在无\n      rewarding exploration下侵蚀SFT patterns。\n      最引人入胜的发现：pruning主效应不显著（p≈0.11）——RASP和Standard\"平均\"差不多。\n      Method主效应也不显著（p≈0.85）——SFT和GRPO\"平均\"差不多。但交互25pp, p<0.001\n      ——pruning选择和recovery方法间存在质变性交互。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Pruning × Recovery Interaction (2×2)\"\n        columns: [Pruning, \"SFT-Only (%)\", \"SFT+GRPO (%)\", \"GRPO Marginal (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP, 58, 70, +12]\n          - [Standard, 66, 53, -13]\n          - [\"RASP Advantage\", -8, +17, \"—\"]\n      - name: \"Interaction ANOVA\"\n        columns: [Effect, \"Estimate (pp)\", SE, p]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pruning (RASP-Std)\", 4.5, 2.8, \"0.11\"]\n          - [\"Method (GRPO-SFT)\", -0.5, 2.7, \"0.85\"]\n          - [\"Pruning × Method\", 25, 3.8, \"0.0008\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2交互图：x=recovery method, y=accuracy, 两条非平行线交叉。Paper Figure 3。\"\n    analysis: >\n      交互p=0.0008直接支持Claim 3。Main effects不显著而interaction显著——optimal\n      pruning取决于recovery method。这是novel finding。\n\n  - name: \"25% Sparsity RASP + Standard\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"25%稀疏度完整pipeline，测试RASP优势在更高压缩下的表现和sparsity scaling。\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_25_post_prune: 0.20\n      standard_25_post_prune: 0.12\n      rasp_25_gap_pp: 8\n      rasp_25_post_sft: 0.42\n      standard_25_post_sft: 0.36\n      rasp_25_post_grpo: 0.55\n      standard_25_post_grpo: 0.32\n      rasp_25_recovery_gap_pp: 23\n      rasp_25_recovery_rate: 0.661\n      standard_25_recovery_rate: 0.385\n    result_rationale: >\n      25%稀疏度放大了post-prune gap（8pp vs 20%的4pp）：额外5%移除不成比例影响\n      Standard——importance-based策略在高稀疏度下被迫移除更多functionally unique\n      groups（它们的importance低），而RASP仍优先保护这些groups。\n      Recovery gap也扩大：23pp(55% vs 32%)，vs 20%的17pp。但amplification factor\n      下降（23/8=2.88x vs 20%的4.25x），因为RASP在25%也开始受损——更多unique\n      groups被迫移除，GRPO redistribution空间缩小。\n      RASP graceful degradation（84→66% recovery rate）vs Standard accelerating\n      collapse（64→39%）支持RASP在多稀疏度下的实用价值。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Multi-Sparsity Comparison\"\n        columns: [Sparsity, Method, \"Post-Prune (%)\", \"Post-GRPO (%)\", \"Recovery (%)\", \"Gap (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"20%\", RASP, 31, 70, 84.1, \"\"]\n          - [\"20%\", Standard, 27, 53, 63.7, 17]\n          - [\"25%\", RASP, 20, 55, 66.1, \"\"]\n          - [\"25%\", Standard, 12, 32, 38.5, 23]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"折线图：sparsity vs recovered accuracy，RASP graceful vs Standard急降。\"\n    analysis: >\n      25%确认RASP优势不是单一操作点artifact。Recovery gap从17→23pp说明CKA-awareness\n      在更高压缩下价值更大。\n\n  - name: \"30% Sparsity Probe\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"30%稀疏度prune+eval only，映射collapse threshold和RASP的操作包络。\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_30_post_prune: 0.08\n      rasp_30_ci95: [0.065, 0.098]\n      standard_30_post_prune: 0.03\n      standard_30_ci95: [0.020, 0.044]\n    result_rationale: >\n      30% RASP降至8%，Standard降至3%。RASP仍非零但已入collapse zone，与D005 35%\n      完全collapse一致。DeepSeek-R1-Distill模型的\"可恢复稀疏度\"上界：~25%有效\n      操作范围，30%边界，35%+崩溃。不进行recovery：8% post-prune的reward signal\n      极稀疏，GRPO难以收敛。Distilled模型的冗余预算天然小于natively-trained模型，\n      因为distillation已经压缩了表示。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Sparsity Collapse Map\"\n        columns: [Sparsity, Method, \"Post-Prune (%)\", Status]\n        rows:\n          - [\"20%\", RASP, 31, Recoverable]\n          - [\"20%\", Standard, 27, Partial]\n          - [\"25%\", RASP, 20, Recoverable]\n          - [\"25%\", Standard, 12, Weak]\n          - [\"30%\", RASP, 8, Near-collapse]\n          - [\"30%\", Standard, 3, Collapsed]\n          - [\"35%\", Both, 0, \"Collapsed (D005)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sparsity曲线20-35%，标注recoverable zone。\"\n    analysis: >\n      完成RASP操作包络映射。Appendix/Discussion材料，回应\"为什么选20%\"。\n\n  - name: \"OOD Evaluation (MATH-500, HumanEval)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Recovered models在GSM8K之外benchmark评估，验证RASP优势的OOD泛化。\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_math500: 0.70\n      rasp_recovered_math500: 0.55\n      standard_recovered_math500: 0.42\n      rasp_math500_advantage_pp: 13\n      baseline_humaneval: 0.50\n      rasp_recovered_humaneval: 0.40\n      standard_recovered_humaneval: 0.33\n      rasp_humaneval_advantage_pp: 7\n      rasp_mean_ood_retention: 0.793\n      standard_mean_ood_retention: 0.630\n    result_rationale: >\n      MATH-500上RASP优势13pp（55% vs 42%），HumanEval上7pp（40% vs 33%）。\n      MATH-500优势更大因为MATH需要更深推理链（多步数学推导），RASP保留的functionally\n      unique结构在深层推理中价值更高。HumanEval更依赖pattern matching/syntax\n      knowledge，pruning影响相对较小。RASP retention: GSM8K 84%, MATH-500 79%,\n      HumanEval 80%——一致~80%+ retention说明RASP保留的是通用推理scaffold而非\n      GSM8K-specific patterns。Standard retention: GSM8K 64%, MATH-500 60%,\n      HumanEval 66%——也一致但低~20pp。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-Benchmark OOD Evaluation\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, \"Baseline (%)\", \"RASP (%)\", \"Standard (%)\", \"RASP Adv. (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [GSM8K, 83.2, 70, 53, 17]\n          - [MATH-500, 70, 55, 42, 13]\n          - [HumanEval, 50, 40, 33, 7]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Radar chart: baseline vs RASP vs Standard，3 benchmarks。\"\n    analysis: >\n      OOD泛化将paper从GSM8K-specific提升为general reasoning compression method。\n      7-17pp一致优势回应reviewer的generalization concern。\n\n  - name: \"Bonsai Baseline at 20% Sparsity\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Bonsai（ICML 2025）gradient-free结构化剪枝。补充external baseline。\"\n    expected_results:\n      bonsai_post_prune: 0.24\n      bonsai_post_sft: 0.50\n      bonsai_post_grpo: 0.47\n      bonsai_grpo_gain_pp: -3\n      bonsai_recovery_rate: 0.565\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bonsai activation-based importance，post-prune 24%略低于Standard 27%（Taylor\n      importance在此模型上稍优，gradient signal捕获了更多推理相关信息）。GRPO对\n      Bonsai也产生负效应（-3pp），与Standard pattern一致：importance-without-CKA\n      方法保留高重叠结构，缺乏GRPO所需的功能独特锚点。4种non-CKA方法中仅GRASPrune\n      从GRPO微弱获益（+3pp，因其gates隐式捕获了部分冗余信息），Standard(-11pp)和\n      Bonsai(-3pp)均受损。GRPO benefit不是普遍现象，而需要CKA-aware结构组成。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Extended Baselines\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Post-Prune (%)\", \"Post-GRPO (%)\", \"GRPO Δ (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP, 31, 70, +13]\n          - [Standard, 27, 53, -11]\n          - [Bonsai, 24, 47, -3]\n          - [GRASPrune, 10, 38, +3]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Bonsai补全baseline方阵。GRPO benefit pattern: RASP(+13) >> GRASPrune(+3) >\n      Bonsai(-3) > Standard(-11)。CKA-awareness是关键区分因素。\n\n  - name: \"CKA Reliability Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Split-half consistency和calibration size sensitivity，CKA scoring可靠性验证。\"\n    expected_results:\n      split_half_rho: 0.93\n      split_half_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      cal_256_gsm8k: 0.29\n      cal_512_gsm8k: 0.31\n      cal_1024_gsm8k: 0.32\n      cal_256_vs_512_rank_corr: 0.90\n      cal_512_vs_1024_rank_corr: 0.97\n      pruned_overlap_256_512: 0.86\n      pruned_overlap_512_1024: 0.95\n    result_rationale: >\n      Split-half ρ=0.93，linear CKA在512样本上已收敛。Calibration size影响微小：\n      256→512提升2pp(29→31%)，512→1024仅1pp(31→32%)，总range 3pp小于inter-seed\n      variance。512是near-optimal calibration size。核心剪枝决策（pruned set\n      overlap 86-95%）对calibration不敏感。Housekeeping but essential for credibility。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"CKA Reliability\"\n        columns: [Analysis, Metric, Value]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Split-half\", \"Spearman ρ\", 0.93]\n          - [\"Cal 256\", \"GSM8K (%)\", 29]\n          - [\"Cal 512\", \"GSM8K (%)\", 31]\n          - [\"Cal 1024\", \"GSM8K (%)\", 32]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"左：split-half scatter。右：calibration sensitivity曲线，plateau at 512。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Appendix材料，main text一行引用。\n\n  - name: \"α Sensitivity Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0}，RASP唯一自由参数的系统性分析。\"\n    expected_results:\n      alpha_0_0: 0.25\n      alpha_0_25: 0.27\n      alpha_0_5: 0.29\n      alpha_1_0: 0.31\n      alpha_2_0: 0.35\n      optimal_alpha: 2.0\n      optimal_vs_alpha0_gap_pp: 10\n      curve_shape: \"monotonically increasing, diminishing returns\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      α=0（importance-only within RASP framework）给出25%，低于Standard 27%。原因：\n      RASP使用reasoning-trace calibration（CoT traces）计算importance，CoT traces\n      较长噪声较高，产生比standard perplexity-calibration稍差的importance estimates。\n      CKA组件补偿并超过差距：α=0.5已达29%（超Standard 27%），α=2.0达35%。\n      曲线单调递增+diminishing returns：0→0.5增4pp，0.5→1.0增2pp，1.0→2.0增4pp\n      （高α端acceleration提示optimal可能>2.0，与预实验α=4.0=40%一致）。\n      最优vs α=0 gap=10pp量化了CKA作为pruning signal的价值。α是唯一free parameter，\n      此ablation为practitioners提供调参指导：α=1合理default，α∈[1,2]推荐范围。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"α Ablation\"\n        columns: [α, Emphasis, \"GSM8K (%)\", \"Δ vs α=0 (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [0.0, \"Importance-only\", 25, 0]\n          - [0.25, \"Weak CKA\", 27, 2]\n          - [0.5, \"Moderate CKA\", 29, 4]\n          - [1.0, \"Balanced (default)\", 31, 6]\n          - [2.0, \"Strong CKA\", 35, 10]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"α vs accuracy曲线，标注Standard(27%)reference line。α>0.3后RASP超Standard。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Dream reviewers全档位Critical实验。10pp gap量化CKA贡献。曲线未见peak说明\n      optimal α可能>2.0，motivates future auto-tuning。\n\n  - name: \"Inference Speedup Benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"Wall-clock latency + throughput比较。结构化剪枝的practical motivation。\"\n    expected_results:\n      dense_latency_ms: 12.4\n      rasp_20_latency_ms: 9.7\n      standard_20_latency_ms: 9.6\n      rasp_20_speedup: 1.28\n      dense_throughput_tok_s: 80.6\n      rasp_20_throughput_tok_s: 103.1\n      memory_reduction_pct: 18.5\n      unstructured_20_speedup: 1.02\n    result_rationale: >\n      20%结构化稀疏度提供1.28x实际加速（12.4→9.7 ms/tok），因为移除200个MLP\n      channel groups直接减少矩阵维度，不需sparse hardware。RASP和Standard speedup\n      几乎相同（均~1.28x），因为两者移除相同数量structures。Memory减少18.5%。\n      对比unstructured 20%（仅1.02x，需sparse tensor cores），structured pruning\n      的practical value明确。RASP在accuracy(70%) + speed(1.28x)两个维度均优于\n      unstructured(60%, 1.02x)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Inference Benchmark\"\n        columns: [Model, \"Latency (ms/tok)\", Speedup, \"Throughput (tok/s)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Dense, 12.4, \"1.00x\", 80.6]\n          - [\"RASP 20%\", 9.7, \"1.28x\", 103.1]\n          - [\"Unstructured 20%\", 12.2, \"1.02x\", 82.0]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"双轴图：latency bars + throughput line。标注structured vs unstructured差异。\"\n    analysis: >\n      1.28x加速 + 70% accuracy提供明确practical motivation。Structured RASP在\n      accuracy和speed两个维度均胜unstructured。\n\n  - name: \"Unstructured Pruning Baseline at 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_017\"\n    description: \"Magnitude-based unstructured 20%。标定structured vs unstructured gap，对标Self-Healing。\"\n    expected_results:\n      unstructured_post_prune: 0.45\n      unstructured_post_sft: 0.55\n      unstructured_post_grpo: 0.60\n      unstructured_grpo_gain_pp: 5\n      unstructured_recovery_rate: 0.721\n      unstructured_speedup: 1.02\n    result_rationale: >\n      Unstructured 20% post-prune 45%远高于structured RASP 31%——保留了所有architectural\n      structures，仅均匀削弱每个structure的capacity。但post-GRPO仅60%，低于RASP 70%。\n      看似反直觉：起点更高却恢复更低。原因：unstructured均匀削弱所有structures，\n      GRPO的redistribution机制在此设置下效率低——没有完整结构可以\"接管\"被削弱结构\n      的功能。RASP的结构化移除创造了明确的donor(移除的高重叠groups)和receiver\n      (保留的独特groups)，GRPO可清晰地将donor功能重分配给receiver。\n      关键比较：RASP structured(70%, 1.28x) vs unstructured(60%, 1.02x)——accuracy\n      和speed双维度RASP占优。对标Self-Healing(2025)的unstructured设置。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Structured vs Unstructured\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Post-Prune (%)\", \"Post-GRPO (%)\", Speedup]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP (structured)\", 31, 70, \"1.28x\"]\n          - [\"Standard (structured)\", 27, 53, \"1.29x\"]\n          - [\"Unstructured 20%\", 45, 60, \"1.02x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: accuracy vs speedup。RASP右上(高accuracy+高speed)，unstructured左下。\"\n    analysis: >\n      RASP structured在accuracy(70>60)和speed(1.28>1.02)双维度优于unstructured。\n      完成\"为什么structured pruning\"论证。\n\n  - name: \"SFT OOD Eval Contingency\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: \"SFT-recovered模型的OOD评估。检验Standard SFT 64%的GSM8K-specificity。\"\n    expected_results:\n      standard_sft_math500: 0.35\n      standard_sft_humaneval: 0.25\n      rasp_sft_math500: 0.42\n      rasp_sft_humaneval: 0.32\n      standard_gsm8k_to_math500_retention: 0.538\n      rasp_gsm8k_to_math500_retention: 0.724\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best tier下GRPO advantage=17pp远超5pp阈值（contingency不strictly needed），\n      但仍提供有价值分析。Standard SFT从GSM8K 66%降至MATH-500 35%（retention 53%），\n      RASP SFT从58%降至42%（retention 72%）。Standard的OOD drop更剧烈：其SFT\n      recovery包含显著GSM8K-specific pattern learning——SFT在高重叠结构上学到了\n      GSM8K特定的数字操作模板，不泛化到MATH。RASP的SFT recovery虽GSM8K绝对数低，\n      但泛化性好，因为functionally unique结构支持更通用推理。\n      补充Claim 3：SFT下Standard的优势是shallow(GSM8K-specific)，GRPO下RASP的\n      优势是deep(OOD-generalizable)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"SFT OOD Transfer\"\n        columns: [Method, \"GSM8K (%)\", \"MATH-500 (%)\", \"HumanEval (%)\", \"MATH Ret. (%)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP SFT-only\", 58, 42, 32, 72.4]\n          - [\"Standard SFT-only\", 66, 35, 25, 53.8]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: GSM8K vs MATH-500 vs HumanEval。Standard GSM8K领先但OOD落后。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Standard SFT优势是shallow，RASP GRPO优势是deep。Discussion增加\"surface vs\n      genuine reasoning recovery\"分析维度。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6569,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39107,"cache_read_input_tokens":29475,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39107},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5a2ac1e-eb55-43b9-94d1-02900c2c612b","uuid":"a3d4c98c-2ab5-4a2e-a3e9-4e41cdd927b3"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":1134259,"duration_api_ms":1135099,"num_turns":5,"result":"Now I have a complete picture of the project state, the existing dream report, actual experimental results, and the best-tier definition. Key calibration points from actual data:\n- reeval_postprune_definitive: RASP=31%, Standard=27% (4pp gap, not 28pp)\n- SFT: RASP=57%, Standard=64% (Standard higher)\n- GRASPrune preliminary: 8% (50 samples)\n- α=4.0 gave 40% post-prune\n\nGenerating the best-tier predictions calibrated to the Recovery Amplification narrative.\n\n```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Recovery Amplification版本：post-prune差异仅4-8pp（31% vs 27%），但GRPO将其\n  放大为17pp recovery gap（70% vs 53%）。更关键的是ranking reversal：SFT下\n  Standard>RASP（66%>58%），GRPO后RASP>>Standard（70%>>53%）。Redundancy Paradox\n  的表现形式不是post-prune的绝对优势，而是GRPO对不同结构组成的差异化响应——\n  GRPO对RASP +12pp，对Standard -13pp。三个claims全部成立：Claim 1修正为\n  \"recovery amplification\"而非\"29x advantage\"；Claim 2的CKA correlation在MLP\n  groups上显著（partial R²=0.22）；Claim 3的排序反转完整成立。GRASPrune打破\n  \"recovery只反映post-prune accuracy\"的线性假设。α ablation给出10pp的CKA贡献\n  量化。OOD eval确认泛化。竞争力：EMNLP Main强投稿，Efficient Methods track。\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K Evaluation (N=1319)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"N=1319全集评估baseline + RASP_20 + Standard_20，替换N=100快速评估，产出publication-quality CI。\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_gsm8k_1319: 0.832\n      baseline_ci95: [0.811, 0.852]\n      rasp_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.31\n      rasp_20_ci95: [0.286, 0.335]\n      standard_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.27\n      standard_20_ci95: [0.246, 0.295]\n      rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 4\n      mcnemar_p: 0.0038\n      rasp_retention_rate: 0.373\n      standard_retention_rate: 0.324\n    result_rationale: >\n      Full N=1319确认reeval_postprune_definitive：RASP 31%、Standard 27%，gap仅4pp。\n      CI从±9pp（N=100）收窄到±2.5pp，McNemar在N=1319下显著（p=0.004）。Baseline\n      83.2%符合DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B的已知GSM8K population accuracy。4pp的\n      post-prune差异表明两种方法保留了相似总量的推理能力，但结构组成不同：RASP保留\n      功能独特的MLP groups（低F(h)锚点），Standard保留高importance的MLP groups（往\n      往高F(h)、高重叠）。这种组成差异在post-prune层面效果有限（4pp），但在GRPO\n      recovery阶段被非线性放大——因为GRPO的redistribution机制对结构多样性的依赖\n      远强于SFT的imitation learning。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Post-Prune GSM8K (N=1319)\"\n        columns: [Method, Sparsity, \"Acc (%)\", \"95% CI\", \"Retention (%)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Baseline, \"0%\", 83.2, \"[81.1, 85.2]\", \"—\"]\n          - [RASP, \"20%\", 31.0, \"[28.6, 33.5]\", 37.3]\n          - [Standard, \"20%\", 27.0, \"[24.6, 29.5]\", 32.4]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"柱状图+95% CI，三个条件。Y轴GSM8K accuracy。4pp gap的CI边缘不重叠。\"\n    analysis: >\n      N=1319确认post-prune gap为4pp且显著。这是Recovery Amplification叙事的起点：\n      小的post-prune差异经过GRPO放大后变成不可逆的recovery gap。\n\n  - name: \"SFT Warmup Recovery\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"RASP_20和Standard_20的SFT warmup恢复。[DONE — 使用实际结果]\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_post_sft: 0.57\n      standard_20_post_sft: 0.64\n      rasp_sft_gain_pp: 26\n      standard_sft_gain_pp: 37\n      rasp_eos_rate: 0.99\n      standard_eos_rate: 0.99\n      rasp_train_loss_final: 0.64\n      standard_train_loss_final: 0.64\n    result_rationale: >\n      [实际结果] Standard SFT(64%) > RASP SFT(57%)，差7pp。SFT通过模仿学习\n      \"扩展\"正确路径（\"SFT Expands\"），偏好高重叠结构——这正是Standard保留的结构\n      类型。Standard的高重叠MLP groups参与多条推理路径，提供了丰富的solution\n      templates供SFT模仿利用。RASP保留的功能独特结构虽然对GRPO redistribution更\n      有利，但在SFT的imitation paradigm下利用效率较低。两者train loss均收敛到0.64、\n      EOS rate 99%，说明SFT学习充分、差异来自结构组成而非训练不充分。Standard SFT\n      优势在N=100下CI重叠（ER-001），不作为Claim 3独立证据，但与GRPO联合构成交互效应。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Post-SFT Warmup\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Post-Prune (%)\", \"Post-SFT (%)\", \"SFT Gain (pp)\", \"EOS Rate\"]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP_20, 31, 57, +26, 0.99]\n          - [Standard_20, 27, 64, +37, 0.99]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"SFT loss曲线对比。两曲线近乎重合（均收敛到0.64），差异来自结构组成非训练动态。\"\n    analysis: >\n      SFT结果锚定了ranking reversal的\"before\"状态：SFT下Standard优于RASP。\n      GRPO（plan_003）需要将此反转。\n\n  - name: \"GRPO Recovery on SFT-Warmed Models\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"GRPO Stage 2恢复。RASP和Standard均从SFT-warmed模型开始，相同超参数和计算预算。核心MVP实验。\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_post_grpo_gsm8k: 0.70\n      rasp_post_grpo_ci95: [0.675, 0.724]\n      standard_post_grpo_gsm8k: 0.53\n      standard_post_grpo_ci95: [0.503, 0.557]\n      grpo_recovery_gap_pp: 17\n      rasp_grpo_gain_over_sft_pp: 13\n      standard_grpo_gain_over_sft_pp: -11\n      rasp_recovery_rate: 0.841\n      standard_recovery_rate: 0.637\n      rasp_reward_mean_final: 0.62\n      standard_reward_mean_final: 0.45\n      rasp_kl_final: 4.1\n      standard_kl_final: 1.8\n      amplification_factor: 4.25\n    result_rationale: >\n      GRPO是Recovery Amplification的核心。RASP 57%→70%（+13pp）：RASP保留的功能\n      独特MLP groups充当GRPO exploration的锚点，编码不可替代的推理子步骤。GRPO通过\n      \"RL Squeezes\"将被剪掉的高重叠groups的功能重新分配到这些锚点。reward从~0.3\n      稳步上升到0.62，KL=4.1表示显著policy移动——模型在积极探索并找到压缩后的推理路径。\n      Standard 64%→53%（-11pp）：GRPO反而伤害了Standard。Standard的高重叠结构为\n      SFT提供了丰富模仿模板（故SFT达64%），但缺乏功能多样性——GRPO exploration在\n      同质化结构空间中找不到有奖励的新路径。KL penalty逐步侵蚀SFT学到的脆弱表面\n      模式，exploration无法补偿损失。reward在0.45震荡（能部分答对但无法持续提升）。\n      核心数字：4pp post-prune gap → 17pp post-GRPO gap，amplification 4.25x。\n      这证明GRPO是非线性过程，对结构组成的依赖远强于SFT。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"SFT→GRPO Recovery Pipeline\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Post-Prune (%)\", \"Post-SFT (%)\", \"Post-GRPO (%)\", \"GRPO Δ (pp)\", \"Recovery (%)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP_20, 31, 57, 70, +13, 84.1]\n          - [Standard_20, 27, 64, 53, -11, 63.7]\n          - [Baseline, 83.2, \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"GRPO reward曲线：RASP稳步上升到0.62，Standard在0.45震荡。\"\n      - \"Waterfall：post-prune→post-SFT→post-GRPO，RASP持续恢复vs Standard的GRPO退化。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Headline result。Ranking reversal完成：SFT下Standard>RASP (64>57)，GRPO后\n      RASP>>Standard (70>>53)。Standard的-11pp GRPO drop是最引人注目的发现——\n      GRPO不仅未帮助Standard，反而主动伤害它。Recovery Amplification confirmed。\n\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K Eval on Recovered Models (N=1319)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"N=1319 bootstrap CI评估所有recovered模型，产出Table 1最终数据。\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_recovered_1319: 0.70\n      rasp_ci95_bootstrap: [0.674, 0.724]\n      standard_recovered_1319: 0.53\n      standard_ci95_bootstrap: [0.503, 0.557]\n      gap_pp: 17\n      cohens_h: 0.35\n      bootstrap_iterations: 10000\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bootstrap CI确认17pp gap统计稳健，CI不重叠。Cohen's h=0.35为中等偏大效应量——\n      不是原始framing的\"巨大\"效应，但17pp在compressed model上是实质性差异（从\n      Standard的勉强可用到RASP的接近baseline性能）。这些数据填入Table 1 \"+SFT+GRPO\"列。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Main Results at 20% Structured Sparsity\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Post-Prune (%)\", \"Post-SFT (%)\", \"Post-SFT+GRPO (%)\", \"Recovery (%)\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Baseline, 83.2, \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"[81.1, 85.2]\"]\n          - [RASP, 31, 57, 70, 84.1, \"[67.4, 72.4]\"]\n          - [Standard, 27, 64, 53, 63.7, \"[50.3, 55.7]\"]\n          - [\"GRASPrune†\", 10, 35, 38, 45.7, \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart：pipeline各阶段accuracy。Paper Figure 1。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Table 1锚定全文。同sparsity、同recovery budget，唯一区别是pruning criterion——\n      RASP的CKA-awareness将recovery rate从64%提升到84%（+20pp）。\n\n  - name: \"GRASPrune Baseline at 20% Sparsity\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"GRASPrune（ACL 2026 SOTA budgeted pruning）完整pipeline。排除recovery-只-反映-post-prune-accuracy的混淆。\"\n    expected_results:\n      grasp_post_prune_gsm8k: 0.10\n      grasp_post_prune_ci95: [0.084, 0.118]\n      grasp_post_sft_gsm8k: 0.35\n      grasp_post_grpo_gsm8k: 0.38\n      grasp_post_grpo_ci95: [0.354, 0.407]\n      grasp_recovery_rate: 0.457\n      grasp_grpo_gain_pp: 3\n      grasp_vs_rasp_recovered_gap_pp: -32\n    result_rationale: >\n      GRASPrune post-prune仅10%（与预实验8%/50样本一致），远低于Standard 27%。这出\n      人意料：GRASPrune的learned gates理论上应优于static Taylor。原因：gates通过\n      reconstruction loss训练，优化\"对语言建模最重要的结构\"而非\"对推理链最重要的\n      结构\"——perplexity-optimal和reasoning-optimal存在系统偏差。\n      关键发现在recovery pattern：GRASPrune 10%→38%（+28pp GRPO gain），Standard\n      27%→53%（+26pp）。GRASPrune起点远低于Standard（-17pp），但GRPO增量略高\n      （+28>+26）。这打破了\"recovery只是post-prune accuracy函数\"的线性假设：如果\n      recovery仅反映post-prune accuracy，GRASPrune应该恢复更少。GRASPrune gates\n      通过梯度流隐式保留了部分功能冗余结构，给GRPO一定redistribution空间，尽管\n      immediate accuracy很差。RASP（+39pp gain，31→70%）远超两者——显式CKA优化\n      比隐式捕获有效得多。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"GRASPrune Pipeline\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Post-Prune (%)\", \"Post-SFT (%)\", \"Post-GRPO (%)\", \"GRPO Gain (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP, 31, 57, 70, +13]\n          - [Standard, 27, 64, 53, -11]\n          - [GRASPrune, 10, 35, 38, +3]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三方法pipeline柱状图。\"\n      - \"Scatter: post-prune accuracy (x) vs GRPO gain (y)，三个点打破线性。\"\n    analysis: >\n      GRASPrune排除两个混淆：(1) RASP优势≠更好的importance estimation（GRASPrune\n      has learned gates yet worse）；(2) recovery≠post-prune accuracy的简单函数。\n      CKA是recovery-optimal pruning的missing ingredient。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-Seed Post-Prune Evaluation (5 Seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"5种子（42,123,7,256,1337）RASP和Standard 20%剪枝+N=1319评估。Post-prune gap的统计稳健性验证。\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_seeds: {42: 0.310, 123: 0.302, 7: 0.321, 256: 0.298, 1337: 0.324}\n      rasp_mean: 0.311\n      rasp_std: 0.011\n      standard_seeds: {42: 0.270, 123: 0.258, 7: 0.275, 256: 0.261, 1337: 0.266}\n      standard_mean: 0.266\n      standard_std: 0.007\n      paired_diffs: [0.040, 0.044, 0.046, 0.037, 0.058]\n      mean_gap_pp: 4.5\n      gap_std_pp: 0.8\n      paired_t_p: 0.0002\n      pruned_set_overlap_range: [0.87, 0.93]\n    result_rationale: >\n      5-seed paired t-test p=0.0002确认4.5pp gap是系统性差异。RASP σ=1.1pp，\n      Standard σ=0.7pp——CKA和Taylor importance在512 calibration样本上已充分收敛。\n      所有5个seed的差异均为正（3.7-5.8pp），无reversal。Pruned set overlap 87-93%\n      表明~180/200 MLP groups跨seed一致，仅14-26个边界groups随calibration变化。\n      稳定性来源：linear CKA是kernel-based statistic，512个mean-pooled activations\n      提供>400有效数据点，远超stable estimation threshold。这排除了\"lucky seed\"和\n      \"calibration artifact\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"5-Seed Robustness\"\n        columns: [Seed, \"RASP (%)\", \"Standard (%)\", \"Gap (pp)\", \"Pruned Set Overlap (%)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [42, 31.0, 27.0, 4.0, \"—\"]\n          - [123, 30.2, 25.8, 4.4, 93]\n          - [7, 32.1, 27.5, 4.6, 89]\n          - [256, 29.8, 26.1, 3.7, 91]\n          - [1337, 32.4, 26.6, 5.8, 87]\n          - [\"Mean±Std\", \"31.1±1.1\", \"26.6±0.7\", \"4.5±0.8\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired strip plot，5 seeds连线。所有连线斜率为正。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Post-prune gap虽小（4.5pp），但5-seed p=0.0002稳健。Claim 1的post-prune\n      component有充分统计支持。\n\n  - name: \"Scoring Ablation at 20% Sparsity\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"RASP评分函数控制消融：magnitude-only, gradient-only, random, CKA-only。隔离各组件贡献。\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_full_gsm8k: 0.31\n      cka_only_gsm8k: 0.29\n      gradient_only_gsm8k: 0.27\n      magnitude_only_gsm8k: 0.25\n      random_gsm8k: 0.18\n    result_rationale: >\n      Post-prune差异较小但系统性：RASP(31%)>CKA-only(29%)>gradient(27%,=Standard)>\n      magnitude(25%)>random(18%)。CKA-only vs gradient仅差2pp，CI部分重叠——在\n      post-prune层面CKA的边际贡献有限。但这恰恰是Recovery Amplification要点：\n      post-prune差异小，GRPO放大差异。Importance贡献（gradient 27% vs random 18%=\n      9pp）在post-prune层面实际上大于CKA边际贡献（CKA-only 29% vs gradient 27%=2pp）。\n      但这个关系在recovery后反转：CKA-aware结构的GRPO recoverability远高于\n      importance-only结构。Random at 18%确认structured scoring确实优于随机。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Scoring Ablation (Post-Prune)\"\n        columns: [Scoring, Formula, \"GSM8K (%)\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP (full)\", \"I(h)×(1-F(h))^α\", 31.0, \"[28.6, 33.5]\"]\n          - [\"CKA-only\", \"(1-F(h))^α\", 29.0, \"[26.6, 31.5]\"]\n          - [\"Gradient-only (=Std)\", \"I(h)\", 27.0, \"[24.6, 29.5]\"]\n          - [\"Magnitude-only\", \"||w_h||₂\", 25.0, \"[22.6, 27.5]\"]\n          - [\"Random\", \"Uniform\", 18.0, \"[15.9, 20.3]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"水平柱状图按accuracy排序。标注Standard baseline reference line (27%)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Post-prune ablation提供组件归因。差异较小但结构清晰。需与recovery数据联合\n      解读——真正的区分在GRPO阶段。\n\n  - name: \"Per-Structure CKA-Recoverability Correlation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"MLP channel group级mixed-effects回归。N=784 MLP groups，layer random effect。控制weight norm/gradient/activation。\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_mlp_groups: 784\n      n_pruned: 200\n      n_layers: 28\n      cka_beta: 0.38\n      cka_se: 0.055\n      cka_t: 6.91\n      cka_p: 0.00034\n      cka_partial_r2: 0.22\n      gradient_beta: 0.12\n      gradient_p: 0.019\n      weight_norm_beta: 0.07\n      weight_norm_p: 0.15\n      activation_beta: 0.04\n      activation_p: 0.42\n      marginal_r2: 0.31\n      conditional_r2: 0.49\n      icc_layer: 0.18\n      vif_max: 2.6\n    result_rationale: >\n      CKA β=0.38 (p=0.0003)在控制weight norm(n.s.)、gradient(marginal p=0.019)、\n      activation(n.s.)后仍显著dominant，partial R²=0.22独立解释22%方差。这是因为\n      CKA overlap直接度量functional redundancy——\"这个MLP group的计算被同层其他\n      groups复制的程度\"——本质上就是\"GRPO能否将被剪group的功能重新分配给剩余groups\"\n      的代理指标。Weight/gradient/activation度量\"当前有多重要\"，不度量\"功能能否\n      被接管\"。ICC=0.18表明层间存在中等聚类：middle layers(8-18)的CKA-recoverability\n      耦合最强（推理redistribution集中于此），与\"RL Squeezes\"机制一致。\n      注意：分析仅在MLP groups(N=784)上进行，20%稀疏度下0/112 attention GQA groups\n      被剪——CKA信号的实际效果是在MLP groups间做reranking。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Mixed-Effects Regression\"\n        columns: [Predictor, \"β (std)\", SE, p, \"Partial R²\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"F(h) CKA overlap\", 0.38, 0.055, \"<0.001\", 0.22]\n          - [\"I(h) gradient\", 0.12, 0.052, 0.019, 0.04]\n          - [\"Weight norm\", 0.07, 0.050, 0.15, 0.01]\n          - [\"Activation mag.\", 0.04, 0.050, 0.42, \"<0.01\"]\n          - [\"Marginal R²\", 0.31, \"\", \"\", \"\"]\n          - [\"Conditional R²\", 0.49, \"\", \"\", \"\"]\n          - [\"ICC (layer)\", 0.18, \"\", \"\", \"\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: per-group F(h) vs recoverability，按layer depth着色，回归线+prediction band。\"\n      - \"Coefficient plot: 4 predictors的95% CI，CKA明确与零分离。\"\n      - \"Caterpillar plot: 28层random effects，middle layers intercept最高。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Claim 2核心证据。CKA(β=0.38)是next-best predictor(gradient β=0.12)的3.2倍，\n      独立解释22%方差。验证了RASP设计理论基础。\n\n  - name: \"SFT-Only Recovery Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"相同pruned模型、相同总计算预算，仅SFT恢复。与plan_003联合构成2×2交互分析，验证Claim 3。\"\n    expected_results:\n      sft_only_rasp: 0.58\n      sft_only_standard: 0.66\n      sft_grpo_rasp: 0.70\n      sft_grpo_standard: 0.53\n      grpo_marginal_rasp_pp: 12\n      grpo_marginal_standard_pp: -13\n      interaction_pp: 25\n      interaction_p: 0.0008\n      rasp_adv_under_sft_pp: -8\n      rasp_adv_under_grpo_pp: 17\n    result_rationale: >\n      Extended SFT（全预算）RASP=58%、Standard=66%，与warmup SFT接近（SFT饱和快）。\n      核心交互：\n      SFT-only: Standard(66%) > RASP(58%) → Standard wins by 8pp\n      SFT+GRPO: RASP(70%) > Standard(53%) → RASP wins by 17pp\n      → 完整ranking reversal。交互效应=12-(-13)=25pp, p=0.0008。\n      机制：\"SFT Expands\"偏好高重叠结构（Standard保留的），模仿学习在多条重叠路径\n      上同时强化。\"RL Squeezes\"需要功能独特锚点（RASP保留的），exploration要求\n      结构多样性来发现新推理路径。Standard缺乏这些锚点，GRPO的KL penalty在无\n      rewarding exploration下侵蚀SFT patterns。\n      最引人入胜的发现：pruning主效应不显著（p≈0.11）——RASP和Standard\"平均\"差不多。\n      Method主效应也不显著（p≈0.85）——SFT和GRPO\"平均\"差不多。但交互25pp, p<0.001\n      ——pruning选择和recovery方法间存在质变性交互。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Pruning × Recovery Interaction (2×2)\"\n        columns: [Pruning, \"SFT-Only (%)\", \"SFT+GRPO (%)\", \"GRPO Marginal (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP, 58, 70, +12]\n          - [Standard, 66, 53, -13]\n          - [\"RASP Advantage\", -8, +17, \"—\"]\n      - name: \"Interaction ANOVA\"\n        columns: [Effect, \"Estimate (pp)\", SE, p]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pruning (RASP-Std)\", 4.5, 2.8, \"0.11\"]\n          - [\"Method (GRPO-SFT)\", -0.5, 2.7, \"0.85\"]\n          - [\"Pruning × Method\", 25, 3.8, \"0.0008\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2交互图：x=recovery method, y=accuracy, 两条非平行线交叉。Paper Figure 3。\"\n    analysis: >\n      交互p=0.0008直接支持Claim 3。Main effects不显著而interaction显著——optimal\n      pruning取决于recovery method。这是novel finding。\n\n  - name: \"25% Sparsity RASP + Standard\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"25%稀疏度完整pipeline，测试RASP优势在更高压缩下的表现和sparsity scaling。\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_25_post_prune: 0.20\n      standard_25_post_prune: 0.12\n      rasp_25_gap_pp: 8\n      rasp_25_post_sft: 0.42\n      standard_25_post_sft: 0.36\n      rasp_25_post_grpo: 0.55\n      standard_25_post_grpo: 0.32\n      rasp_25_recovery_gap_pp: 23\n      rasp_25_recovery_rate: 0.661\n      standard_25_recovery_rate: 0.385\n    result_rationale: >\n      25%稀疏度放大了post-prune gap（8pp vs 20%的4pp）：额外5%移除不成比例影响\n      Standard——importance-based策略在高稀疏度下被迫移除更多functionally unique\n      groups（它们的importance低），而RASP仍优先保护这些groups。\n      Recovery gap也扩大：23pp(55% vs 32%)，vs 20%的17pp。但amplification factor\n      下降（23/8=2.88x vs 20%的4.25x），因为RASP在25%也开始受损——更多unique\n      groups被迫移除，GRPO redistribution空间缩小。\n      RASP graceful degradation（84→66% recovery rate）vs Standard accelerating\n      collapse（64→39%）支持RASP在多稀疏度下的实用价值。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Multi-Sparsity Comparison\"\n        columns: [Sparsity, Method, \"Post-Prune (%)\", \"Post-GRPO (%)\", \"Recovery (%)\", \"Gap (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"20%\", RASP, 31, 70, 84.1, \"\"]\n          - [\"20%\", Standard, 27, 53, 63.7, 17]\n          - [\"25%\", RASP, 20, 55, 66.1, \"\"]\n          - [\"25%\", Standard, 12, 32, 38.5, 23]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"折线图：sparsity vs recovered accuracy，RASP graceful vs Standard急降。\"\n    analysis: >\n      25%确认RASP优势不是单一操作点artifact。Recovery gap从17→23pp说明CKA-awareness\n      在更高压缩下价值更大。\n\n  - name: \"30% Sparsity Probe\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"30%稀疏度prune+eval only，映射collapse threshold和RASP的操作包络。\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_30_post_prune: 0.08\n      rasp_30_ci95: [0.065, 0.098]\n      standard_30_post_prune: 0.03\n      standard_30_ci95: [0.020, 0.044]\n    result_rationale: >\n      30% RASP降至8%，Standard降至3%。RASP仍非零但已入collapse zone，与D005 35%\n      完全collapse一致。DeepSeek-R1-Distill模型的\"可恢复稀疏度\"上界：~25%有效\n      操作范围，30%边界，35%+崩溃。不进行recovery：8% post-prune的reward signal\n      极稀疏，GRPO难以收敛。Distilled模型的冗余预算天然小于natively-trained模型，\n      因为distillation已经压缩了表示。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Sparsity Collapse Map\"\n        columns: [Sparsity, Method, \"Post-Prune (%)\", Status]\n        rows:\n          - [\"20%\", RASP, 31, Recoverable]\n          - [\"20%\", Standard, 27, Partial]\n          - [\"25%\", RASP, 20, Recoverable]\n          - [\"25%\", Standard, 12, Weak]\n          - [\"30%\", RASP, 8, Near-collapse]\n          - [\"30%\", Standard, 3, Collapsed]\n          - [\"35%\", Both, 0, \"Collapsed (D005)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sparsity曲线20-35%，标注recoverable zone。\"\n    analysis: >\n      完成RASP操作包络映射。Appendix/Discussion材料，回应\"为什么选20%\"。\n\n  - name: \"OOD Evaluation (MATH-500, HumanEval)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Recovered models在GSM8K之外benchmark评估，验证RASP优势的OOD泛化。\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_math500: 0.70\n      rasp_recovered_math500: 0.55\n      standard_recovered_math500: 0.42\n      rasp_math500_advantage_pp: 13\n      baseline_humaneval: 0.50\n      rasp_recovered_humaneval: 0.40\n      standard_recovered_humaneval: 0.33\n      rasp_humaneval_advantage_pp: 7\n      rasp_mean_ood_retention: 0.793\n      standard_mean_ood_retention: 0.630\n    result_rationale: >\n      MATH-500上RASP优势13pp（55% vs 42%），HumanEval上7pp（40% vs 33%）。\n      MATH-500优势更大因为MATH需要更深推理链（多步数学推导），RASP保留的functionally\n      unique结构在深层推理中价值更高。HumanEval更依赖pattern matching/syntax\n      knowledge，pruning影响相对较小。RASP retention: GSM8K 84%, MATH-500 79%,\n      HumanEval 80%——一致~80%+ retention说明RASP保留的是通用推理scaffold而非\n      GSM8K-specific patterns。Standard retention: GSM8K 64%, MATH-500 60%,\n      HumanEval 66%——也一致但低~20pp。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-Benchmark OOD Evaluation\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, \"Baseline (%)\", \"RASP (%)\", \"Standard (%)\", \"RASP Adv. (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [GSM8K, 83.2, 70, 53, 17]\n          - [MATH-500, 70, 55, 42, 13]\n          - [HumanEval, 50, 40, 33, 7]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Radar chart: baseline vs RASP vs Standard，3 benchmarks。\"\n    analysis: >\n      OOD泛化将paper从GSM8K-specific提升为general reasoning compression method。\n      7-17pp一致优势回应reviewer的generalization concern。\n\n  - name: \"Bonsai Baseline at 20% Sparsity\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Bonsai（ICML 2025）gradient-free结构化剪枝。补充external baseline。\"\n    expected_results:\n      bonsai_post_prune: 0.24\n      bonsai_post_sft: 0.50\n      bonsai_post_grpo: 0.47\n      bonsai_grpo_gain_pp: -3\n      bonsai_recovery_rate: 0.565\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bonsai activation-based importance，post-prune 24%略低于Standard 27%（Taylor\n      importance在此模型上稍优，gradient signal捕获了更多推理相关信息）。GRPO对\n      Bonsai也产生负效应（-3pp），与Standard pattern一致：importance-without-CKA\n      方法保留高重叠结构，缺乏GRPO所需的功能独特锚点。4种non-CKA方法中仅GRASPrune\n      从GRPO微弱获益（+3pp，因其gates隐式捕获了部分冗余信息），Standard(-11pp)和\n      Bonsai(-3pp)均受损。GRPO benefit不是普遍现象，而需要CKA-aware结构组成。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Extended Baselines\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Post-Prune (%)\", \"Post-GRPO (%)\", \"GRPO Δ (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP, 31, 70, +13]\n          - [Standard, 27, 53, -11]\n          - [Bonsai, 24, 47, -3]\n          - [GRASPrune, 10, 38, +3]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Bonsai补全baseline方阵。GRPO benefit pattern: RASP(+13) >> GRASPrune(+3) >\n      Bonsai(-3) > Standard(-11)。CKA-awareness是关键区分因素。\n\n  - name: \"CKA Reliability Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Split-half consistency和calibration size sensitivity，CKA scoring可靠性验证。\"\n    expected_results:\n      split_half_rho: 0.93\n      split_half_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      cal_256_gsm8k: 0.29\n      cal_512_gsm8k: 0.31\n      cal_1024_gsm8k: 0.32\n      cal_256_vs_512_rank_corr: 0.90\n      cal_512_vs_1024_rank_corr: 0.97\n      pruned_overlap_256_512: 0.86\n      pruned_overlap_512_1024: 0.95\n    result_rationale: >\n      Split-half ρ=0.93，linear CKA在512样本上已收敛。Calibration size影响微小：\n      256→512提升2pp(29→31%)，512→1024仅1pp(31→32%)，总range 3pp小于inter-seed\n      variance。512是near-optimal calibration size。核心剪枝决策（pruned set\n      overlap 86-95%）对calibration不敏感。Housekeeping but essential for credibility。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"CKA Reliability\"\n        columns: [Analysis, Metric, Value]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Split-half\", \"Spearman ρ\", 0.93]\n          - [\"Cal 256\", \"GSM8K (%)\", 29]\n          - [\"Cal 512\", \"GSM8K (%)\", 31]\n          - [\"Cal 1024\", \"GSM8K (%)\", 32]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"左：split-half scatter。右：calibration sensitivity曲线，plateau at 512。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Appendix材料，main text一行引用。\n\n  - name: \"α Sensitivity Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0}，RASP唯一自由参数的系统性分析。\"\n    expected_results:\n      alpha_0_0: 0.25\n      alpha_0_25: 0.27\n      alpha_0_5: 0.29\n      alpha_1_0: 0.31\n      alpha_2_0: 0.35\n      optimal_alpha: 2.0\n      optimal_vs_alpha0_gap_pp: 10\n      curve_shape: \"monotonically increasing, diminishing returns\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      α=0（importance-only within RASP framework）给出25%，低于Standard 27%。原因：\n      RASP使用reasoning-trace calibration（CoT traces）计算importance，CoT traces\n      较长噪声较高，产生比standard perplexity-calibration稍差的importance estimates。\n      CKA组件补偿并超过差距：α=0.5已达29%（超Standard 27%），α=2.0达35%。\n      曲线单调递增+diminishing returns：0→0.5增4pp，0.5→1.0增2pp，1.0→2.0增4pp\n      （高α端acceleration提示optimal可能>2.0，与预实验α=4.0=40%一致）。\n      最优vs α=0 gap=10pp量化了CKA作为pruning signal的价值。α是唯一free parameter，\n      此ablation为practitioners提供调参指导：α=1合理default，α∈[1,2]推荐范围。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"α Ablation\"\n        columns: [α, Emphasis, \"GSM8K (%)\", \"Δ vs α=0 (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [0.0, \"Importance-only\", 25, 0]\n          - [0.25, \"Weak CKA\", 27, 2]\n          - [0.5, \"Moderate CKA\", 29, 4]\n          - [1.0, \"Balanced (default)\", 31, 6]\n          - [2.0, \"Strong CKA\", 35, 10]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"α vs accuracy曲线，标注Standard(27%)reference line。α>0.3后RASP超Standard。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Dream reviewers全档位Critical实验。10pp gap量化CKA贡献。曲线未见peak说明\n      optimal α可能>2.0，motivates future auto-tuning。\n\n  - name: \"Inference Speedup Benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"Wall-clock latency + throughput比较。结构化剪枝的practical motivation。\"\n    expected_results:\n      dense_latency_ms: 12.4\n      rasp_20_latency_ms: 9.7\n      standard_20_latency_ms: 9.6\n      rasp_20_speedup: 1.28\n      dense_throughput_tok_s: 80.6\n      rasp_20_throughput_tok_s: 103.1\n      memory_reduction_pct: 18.5\n      unstructured_20_speedup: 1.02\n    result_rationale: >\n      20%结构化稀疏度提供1.28x实际加速（12.4→9.7 ms/tok），因为移除200个MLP\n      channel groups直接减少矩阵维度，不需sparse hardware。RASP和Standard speedup\n      几乎相同（均~1.28x），因为两者移除相同数量structures。Memory减少18.5%。\n      对比unstructured 20%（仅1.02x，需sparse tensor cores），structured pruning\n      的practical value明确。RASP在accuracy(70%) + speed(1.28x)两个维度均优于\n      unstructured(60%, 1.02x)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Inference Benchmark\"\n        columns: [Model, \"Latency (ms/tok)\", Speedup, \"Throughput (tok/s)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Dense, 12.4, \"1.00x\", 80.6]\n          - [\"RASP 20%\", 9.7, \"1.28x\", 103.1]\n          - [\"Unstructured 20%\", 12.2, \"1.02x\", 82.0]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"双轴图：latency bars + throughput line。标注structured vs unstructured差异。\"\n    analysis: >\n      1.28x加速 + 70% accuracy提供明确practical motivation。Structured RASP在\n      accuracy和speed两个维度均胜unstructured。\n\n  - name: \"Unstructured Pruning Baseline at 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_017\"\n    description: \"Magnitude-based unstructured 20%。标定structured vs unstructured gap，对标Self-Healing。\"\n    expected_results:\n      unstructured_post_prune: 0.45\n      unstructured_post_sft: 0.55\n      unstructured_post_grpo: 0.60\n      unstructured_grpo_gain_pp: 5\n      unstructured_recovery_rate: 0.721\n      unstructured_speedup: 1.02\n    result_rationale: >\n      Unstructured 20% post-prune 45%远高于structured RASP 31%——保留了所有architectural\n      structures，仅均匀削弱每个structure的capacity。但post-GRPO仅60%，低于RASP 70%。\n      看似反直觉：起点更高却恢复更低。原因：unstructured均匀削弱所有structures，\n      GRPO的redistribution机制在此设置下效率低——没有完整结构可以\"接管\"被削弱结构\n      的功能。RASP的结构化移除创造了明确的donor(移除的高重叠groups)和receiver\n      (保留的独特groups)，GRPO可清晰地将donor功能重分配给receiver。\n      关键比较：RASP structured(70%, 1.28x) vs unstructured(60%, 1.02x)——accuracy\n      和speed双维度RASP占优。对标Self-Healing(2025)的unstructured设置。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Structured vs Unstructured\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Post-Prune (%)\", \"Post-GRPO (%)\", Speedup]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP (structured)\", 31, 70, \"1.28x\"]\n          - [\"Standard (structured)\", 27, 53, \"1.29x\"]\n          - [\"Unstructured 20%\", 45, 60, \"1.02x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: accuracy vs speedup。RASP右上(高accuracy+高speed)，unstructured左下。\"\n    analysis: >\n      RASP structured在accuracy(70>60)和speed(1.28>1.02)双维度优于unstructured。\n      完成\"为什么structured pruning\"论证。\n\n  - name: \"SFT OOD Eval Contingency\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: \"SFT-recovered模型的OOD评估。检验Standard SFT 64%的GSM8K-specificity。\"\n    expected_results:\n      standard_sft_math500: 0.35\n      standard_sft_humaneval: 0.25\n      rasp_sft_math500: 0.42\n      rasp_sft_humaneval: 0.32\n      standard_gsm8k_to_math500_retention: 0.538\n      rasp_gsm8k_to_math500_retention: 0.724\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best tier下GRPO advantage=17pp远超5pp阈值（contingency不strictly needed），\n      但仍提供有价值分析。Standard SFT从GSM8K 66%降至MATH-500 35%（retention 53%），\n      RASP SFT从58%降至42%（retention 72%）。Standard的OOD drop更剧烈：其SFT\n      recovery包含显著GSM8K-specific pattern learning——SFT在高重叠结构上学到了\n      GSM8K特定的数字操作模板，不泛化到MATH。RASP的SFT recovery虽GSM8K绝对数低，\n      但泛化性好，因为functionally unique结构支持更通用推理。\n      补充Claim 3：SFT下Standard的优势是shallow(GSM8K-specific)，GRPO下RASP的\n      优势是deep(OOD-generalizable)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"SFT OOD Transfer\"\n        columns: [Method, \"GSM8K (%)\", \"MATH-500 (%)\", \"HumanEval (%)\", \"MATH Ret. (%)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP SFT-only\", 58, 42, 32, 72.4]\n          - [\"Standard SFT-only\", 66, 35, 25, 53.8]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: GSM8K vs MATH-500 vs HumanEval。Standard GSM8K领先但OOD落后。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Standard SFT优势是shallow，RASP GRPO优势是deep。Discussion增加\"surface vs\n      genuine reasoning recovery\"分析维度。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d5a2ac1e-eb55-43b9-94d1-02900c2c612b","total_cost_usd":1.9943277000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":6572,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56741,"cache_read_input_tokens":66292,"output_tokens":55127,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56741,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6569,"output_tokens":54528,"cache_read_input_tokens":29475,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39107,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39107},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":8137,"outputTokens":6323,"cacheReadInputTokens":302497,"cacheCreationInputTokens":100411,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.19551545,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":6572,"outputTokens":55127,"cacheReadInputTokens":66292,"cacheCreationInputTokens":56741,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.7988122500000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"60e8e5f4-eaaa-4fc4-bce1-806a58f53250"}
